        "policy": "Equity & Net Worth Lending",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] #### Equity Program ####\r\n* Our Equity Program helps to ensure your clients have access to mortgage solutions tailored to their unique situations. \r\n**Overview**\r\nThe borrower must have stable to moderate confirmable income. \r\n**Program Features**\r\nThis solution is ideal for salaried or self-employed borrowers seeking to purchase or refinance a marketable property where there is a large equity or down payment position. Borrowers may have debt service ratios that may not necessarily fit standard requirements and may be elevated. \r\n**Property type**\r\n* 1 \u2013 4 units, owner occupied principal residence \r\n* The collateral must comply with the neighbourhood and be well maintained (to be assessed on a case by case basis) \r\n* No deferred maintenance \r\n* Property to be in an urban area with municipal services (to be assessed on a case by case basis) \r\n**Lending areas and loan amounts**\r\n- Contact your Business Development Manager for more information.\r\n**Max amortization**\r\n- 30 years\r\n**Credit Score & LTV**\r\n* 680\r\n**LTV, Beacon and TDS limits**\r\n\u2022 Equity 50 \u2013 50% LTV max. credit score 680+, max. TDS 65% \r\n\u2022 Equity 65 \u2013 65% LTV max. credit score 720+, max. TDS 60% \r\n**Other Conditions**\r\n* Standard income validation applies\r\n* Owner-occupied \r\n* Primary residence \r\n* Full appraisal \r\n* No gifted down payment \r\n* No POA \r\n* No previous bankruptcy, consumer proposal, orderly payment of debt and credit counselling \r\n* No income tax arrears \r\n* No delinquencies \r\n#### Net Worth Program #### \r\n* The Net Worth Program is designed for clients with moderate income who can demonstrate sufficient proven liquid assets and maintain satisfactory credit scores.\r\n**Property Occupancy**\r\n* Owner-occupied: 1\u20134 units\r\n* Second/vacation home: 1\u20132 units\r\n* The program allows eligibility for up to two properties:\r\n* One owner-occupied\r\n* One second or vacation home\r\n**Loan and Qualification Parameters**\r\n* Minimum Credit Score 650\r\n* Maximum Amortization 30 years\r\n* Maximum TDS 70%\r\n* Maximum LTV 65%\r\n* Minimum Liquid Assets $150,000\r\n**Additional guidelines:**\r\n* Standard income validation applies.\r\n* Minimum annual total income: $18,000 (can include full-time, part-time, contractual, self-employed, retirement, etc.).\r\n* Income cannot consist solely of rental income, Canada Child Benefit, child, or spousal support.\r\n* Net rental income may count for up to 50% of total income.\r\n* If income is derived from RRSPs, RRIFs, or other investment assets, those assets cannot also be used as qualifying liquid assets (no double dipping).\r\n* Exceptions to the 70% TDS limit require Underwriting Manager approval.\r\n**Amortization and Terms*\r\n* Amortization:\r\n* Maximum 30 years (no extended terms for rentals specified in the new update).\r\n**Terms Available:**\r\n* 1\u20135 years, 7 years, and 10-year closed\r\n* 3- and 5-year VRM\r\n**Other Program Conditions**\r\n* No Power of Attorney permitted.\r\n* No previous bankruptcy, consumer proposal, or major derogatory credit.\r\n* No payment arrears.\r\n* Only Canadian residents claiming taxes in Canada are eligible.\r\n* No gifted down payment.\r\n* Full property appraisal required.\r\n* Not available under the Homeowner\u2019s Kit (HOK).\r\n* All account holders must appear on the mortgage application.\r\n* Personal guarantors are allowed only in spousal situations.\r\n**Eligible Proven Liquid Assets**\r\n* Publicly traded stocks (TSX, S&P 500, Dow Jones Industrial Average, NASDAQ)\r\n* Canadian Savings Bonds\r\n* GICs\r\n* Chequing and savings accounts (business accounts not admissible)\r\n* RESPs (capital only)\r\n* TFSAs\r\n* Retirement accounts (discounted by 30% for withholding tax)\r\n* Equity in a property being sold (firm purchase & sale agreement required)\r\n* Mutual funds\r\n* ESOP (if publicly traded)\r\n* RRIFs\r\n* Investments in U.S. currency are acceptable if held within Canada. Bank of Canada exchange rates will apply for qualification purposes.\r\n**Ineligible Assets**\r\n* Locked-in accounts\r\n* Foreign assets\r\n* Cryptocurrency\r\n* Assets held in a business name (cash, retained earnings, investments, holdings, etc.)\r\n* Shares in private companies\r\n* Equity in properties not being sold (Applies: National)",
