        "policy": "Credit History: Bruised credit, consumer proposals, bankruptcy",
        "description": "* Bankruptcy (BK), Consumer Proposal (CP), Orderly Payment of Debt (OPD) and Credit Counselling (CC)\r\n* Applications will be cautiously considered when a borrower has experienced a BK, CP, OPD or CC.\r\n* The reason for the BK, CP, OPD and CC must be documented in the file.\r\n* The reason for the BK, CP, OPD and CC must be an acceptable event, for example business failure or marital split, rather than mismanagement.\r\n* The mortgage underwriter must clearly state why the reason for this is acceptable and unlikely to repeat.\r\n* Only one occurrence is acceptable; this includes BK, CP, OPD or CC.\r\n* Prime and Near Prime Mortgage Requirements (A Side):\r\n* BK Requirements:\r\n* Two years or more since discharge. Confirmation of the discharge date is required on file. The mortgage underwriter can use the credit report or obtain a copy of the discharge statement and the statement of affairs.\r\n* Credit bureau report confirms no late payments in the 12 months prior to the date of submission.\r\n* Eligible re-established credit for a minimum of 12 months from the date of discharge: term loan, instalment loan, mortgage loan, car lease or 2 revolving credits with minimum limits of $1,000 each.\r\nCP, OPD and CC Requirements:\r\n* Six month or more since discharge. Confirmation of the discharge date is required on file. The mortgage underwriter can use the credit report or obtain a copy of the discharge statement and the statement of affairs.\r\n* Confirmation of no late payments for a minimum of 12 months prior to the date of submission.\r\n* Eligible re-established credit: term loan, instalment loan, mortgage loan, car lease or 2 revolving credits with minimum limits of $1,000 each (Applies: National)",
