        "policy": "Qualifying Rates",
        "description": "- **Effective November 21, 2024:**\r\n - OSFI no longer requires the Minimum Qualifying Rate (MQR) for uninsured mortgage borrowers switching institutions at renewal.\r\n - Coast Capital will apply an internal stress test aligned with OSFI B20 guidelines.\r\n- **Eligibility Criteria for Transfers to Coast Capital:**\r\n - Must occur at renewal.\r\n - Coast Capital's appropriate minimum qualifying rate will be applied (details below).\r\n - No changes to the borrower(s).\r\n - No increase to the balance or remaining contractual amortization.\r\n - Up to $3,000 may be added to the mortgage balance to cover transaction costs.\r\n - Mortgage must originate from a Federally Regulated Financial Institution.\r\n- **Qualifying Rates:**\r\n - **Fixed Mortgage Terms (3 Years or Greater):**\r\n - Minimum qualifying rate = contractual rate.\r\n - **Variable Mortgage Terms and Fixed Terms Under 3 Years:**\r\n - Minimum qualifying rate = greater of the contractual rate or Coast Capital's current posted 5-year fixed member rate (25-year amortization).\r\n- **HELOCs and Combined Loan Plans:**\r\n - Not eligible for transfer without applying the OSFI MQR stress test.\r\n - Additional sub-advances are allowed if the OSFI MQR stress test is applied to the new advance(s).\r\n- **Insurable Product Eligibility:**\r\n - Straight mortgage transfer-ins meeting the criteria are eligible for Coast Capital\u2019s Insurable product (Applies: British Columbia)",
