        "id": 88,
        "policy": "Submission Tips & Underwriting Assistance",
        "description": "* Yes, TransUnion accepted\r\n* Applications lacking the minimum required document package will not be considered for underwriting.\r\n* Incomplete submissions will be promptly cancelled and returned, removing them from the underwriting queue.\r\n* All documents should be sent to brokercentre@coastcapitalsavings.com or submitted via the lender portal. Please refrain from emailing documents directly to the Underwriter.\r\n* When submitting documents for purchase applications, kindly include the Subject Removal Date and Client Name in the subject line.\r\n* Refinance/transfer in submissions where the mortgage is up for renewal it's crucial to make arrangements that this renews into an open term\r\n* Please specify if the mortgage is \"Insurable\" or \"FCT required\" in your comments.\r\n* Rate holds will not be provided for cancelled submissions.\r\n* An email confirmation will be sent once your deal has been added to our queue. Please note this can take up to 10 business days\r\n* ***Rush applications can not be accommodated***\r\n**Purchase Submission**\r\n* Current income documents this includes confirmation of rental income\r\n* Purchase agreement (including Property Disclosure Statement, any Addendums or Assignment Contracts if applicable)\r\n* MLS listing.\r\n* 60 day confirmation of down payment\r\n * Verification of Down Payment as applicable: \r\n * Where any portion of the down payment is from savings in bank account \u2013 a 60 day account history is required\r\n * if 60 day history shows a wire transfer in, provide details on source of funds (i.e. where are funds from (location)) and how they were acquired (i.e. sale of property, etc.)\r\n * Identify any gifted portion \u2013 noting a signed Gift Letter can be a condition of approval\r\n * Sales Contract \u2013 if from sale of property (MLS if listed and not yet sold)\r\n * Draft confirming deposit amount\r\n* 12 months of strata minutes and most recent AGM for High Ratio strata property applications only\r\n* For pre-sale purchases completing within 90 days please also provide one of the following:\r\n * Confirmation of completion from the developer. The confirmation of completion notice can be in form of an email or letter noting the property will be complete within 90 days of this submission. \r\n * Confirmation of walkthrough date from the Developer\r\n**Refinance Documentation**\r\n* Current income documents* this includes confirmation of rental income\r\n* Current mortgage statement (if mortgage not reporting on bureau)\r\n* If mortgage is currently insured by CMHC or Sagen, please include the certification #\r\n* Title search for subject property (FCT Refinances)\r\n* Current fire insurance policy (FCT Refinances)\r\n**Current Members**\r\n* During the heavy spring season, priority is given if you are a current member\r\n* **CMHC/Sagen Insured Purchases:** Please allow a minimum of 5 business days for subject removal, with completion within 15+ days.\r\n* **Insurable/Conventional Purchases:** Allow at least 10 business days for subject removal, with completion within 15+ days. (Applies: British Columbia)",
        "isAccepted": null
