        "id": 92,
        "policy": "Types of Financing",
        "description": "Transfer/Switch\r\n* Insured & Insurable\r\nMulti-Purpose Mortgage\r\n* You can split a mortgage into sections, each with its own term length and interest rate. HELOC's also available as a section.\r\n* You can even borrow up to 80% of a home\u2019s equity. HELOC portion max 65%of the 80% LTV.\r\n* Flexible pre-payment options: Up to 20% per year on the anniversary date only and up to double payments on regular payment dates\r\nCMHC/Sagen Insured Mortgages\r\n* Eligible for a standard or Multi-Purpose Mortgage\r\n* Best rates available for all CMHC and Sagen insured mortgages\r\n* Maximum LTV \u2013 95% for purchase and 80% for refinancing\r\n* Purchase price must be below $1,000,000\r\n* Maximum amortization \u2013 25 years\r\n* Maximum GDS/TDS as allowed by the insurer\r\n* Use of rental income as allowed by the insurer \r\n* Sagen and CMHC insured mortgages that qualify for the new 30-year amortization at the same rate as our 25-year amortization options. \r\nConventional Mortgages - Owner Occupied\r\n* Eligible for a standard, Multi-Purpose Mortgage\r\n* Maximum LTV ratio \u2013 80% of the 1st $1,000,000 and 65% of the remaining value (based on appraised value). Revolving HELOC portion cannot exceed 65% LTV\r\n* Maximum GDS/TDS ratio:\r\n* 39/44% for beacons 680+\r\n* 35/42% for beacons 620 - 679\r\n* Maximum amortization \u2013 30 years\r\n* 100% add back to income excluding taxes and heat for suite income (up to 2 suites)\r\n* Maximum mortgage $2,500,000\r\n* Qualify using the Stress Test\r\nConventional Mortgages - Rental Properties\r\n* Eligible for a standard or Multi-Purpose Mortgage\r\n* Maximum LTV ratio \u2013 80% of the 1st $1,000,000 and 65% of the remaining value (based on appraised value). Revolving HELOC portion cannot exceed 65% LTV\r\n* Maximum GDS/TDS ratio\r\n* 39/44% for beacons 680+\r\n* 35/42% for beacons 620 - 679\r\n* Maximum amortization \u2013 30 years\r\n* For both subject and non subject rental properties, rental income is calculated based on the following:\r\n* Net rental income = Gross Rental Income - Expenses [Payments + Property Taxes +50% of Strata + Vacancy Allowance (5%) + Property Maintenance (15%)]\r\n* Maximum mortgage $2,500,000\r\n* Qualify using the Stress Test. (Applies: British Columbia)",
