        "id": 48,
        "policy": "Income - BFS (Other BFS Programs, Bank Statement etc)",
        "description": "**NEW! EXTENDED RATIO PROGRAM \u2013 60/60 GDS/TDS**\r\n- **No Rate Premium** from our standard rates. \r\n- Available for **Owner-Occupied** and **Rental Properties**. \r\n- **Minimum Beacon Score:** \r\n - 670 for general eligibility. \r\n - 720+ required for **80% LTV**. \r\n- **Amortization:** 30 years. \r\n- **Maximum Mortgage Amount:** $1.5M. \r\n- **Rental Premium:** 0.50%. \r\n**Income Requirements:** \r\n- For **owner-occupied properties**, qualifying income must be **>50% BFS**. \r\n- For **rental properties**, **100% salaried income** is acceptable. \r\n**Program Availability:** \r\n- Offered in **Ontario**, **British Columbia**, and **Alberta**. \r\n- In Alberta, only available in **Calgary** and **Edmonton**. \r\n- **Certain geographic restrictions apply**. \r\n***Calculating Stated Income***\r\nGross Income - Total Expenses = Stated Income \r\n1. **Add up all business deposits** within 12 months of bank statements. \r\n2. **Deduct all business withdrawals/expenses** from the 12-month bank statements. \r\n**Deposits - Expenses = Net Stated Annual Income** \r\n**TIP:** Look for recurring withdrawals on the statements, which will be counted as expenses. \r\n**Common Expenses to Look For:** \r\n- Fuel \r\n- Car payments \r\n- Insurance \r\n- Purchase orders/Cost of goods \r\n- Rent \r\n- Wages for employees \r\n- Bank fees \r\n- Cell phone \r\n- Internet \r\n**Example:** \r\nIf gross annual revenue is $120,000 and total expenses are $40,000, then the net annual income used to qualify will be **$80,000**. \r\nWe don\u2019t impose any fixed percentage of expenses, as we understand the nature of every business is different. However, we ask that the expenses used are reasonable based on the business type. \r\n---\r\n**Documentation Required** \r\nProof of 2 years of business ownership, confirmed by ONE of the following: \r\n- Articles of Incorporation \r\n- Valid Business License \r\n- Commission sales letter or employment contract confirming the commission arrangement \r\n- Signed income declaration letter ([click link here]) \r\nThe declared income must be supported by: \r\n- 12-months of bank statements \r\n- Sales order contracts, 4\u20136 invoices to match business statement deposits, OR employment contract \r\n**Note:** Please indicate the full company name and the nature of the client\u2019s business. \r\n--- (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
