        "id": 75,
        "policy": "Submission Tips & Underwriting Assistance",
        "description": "* Yes, TransUnion accepted\r\n**SignUp**\r\n- All individuals with a license must register with FN to work with us. Our registration link is on our website (https://brokers.firstnational.ca/)\r\n- Everyone has their own individual profile, and the expectation is that when they submit, the \u201cagent\u201d is in the \u201cagent profile,\u201d and their pooling broker is the \u201csubmission agent.\u201d\r\n**Stated Income Template Notes Template**\r\n- Name of the business the company operates under (numbered company alone is insufficient): \r\n- Nature of the business: \r\n- Number of years in business: \r\n- Number of employees (PT/FT): \r\n- Physical address of the business: \r\n- Area to which the business services: \r\n- E-address of the business (website/411): \r\n- Sole Prop / Partnership / Inc : \r\n- Percentage of ownership: \r\n- Brief description of how the business generates income: \r\n- Line 150 income amount from most recent tax year: \r\n- Gross business earnings\r\n**Down Payment Notes (Merlin Uploads)**\r\n* When uploading documents into Merlin, the email body must include a clear summary outlining:\r\n* Which accounts hold which funds.\r\n* How the down payment and closing costs are allocated across accounts.\r\n* Clear notes significantly reduce follow-ups and processing delays.\r\n**Gifted Down Payments**\r\n* For gifted funds, please include:\r\n* A signed First National Gift Letter, and\r\n* Proof of the gifted funds being deposited into the client\u2019s account.\r\n**Out-of-Country Funds**\r\n* For down payments sourced from outside Canada, please contact your Account Manager to discuss the specific scenario before submission.\r\n**Closing Costs**\r\n* Ensure the file clearly accounts for the full down payment plus an additional 1.5% for closing costs. (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
