        "id": 22,
        "policy": "Purchase Plus Improvement & Refinance Plus Improvement",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Down Payment**\r\n- Minimum of 5% required based on the \u2018as improved\u2019 value of the property.\r\n**PPI Highlights**\r\n- Maximum improvements limited to the lesser of $100,000 or 20% of the \u2018as is\u2019 value of the property\r\n- PPI can be from $5K \u2013 $100K, exceptions and beyond may be considered\r\nImprovements must be supported to have $1 for $1 value appreciation\r\n- Structural changes may require development and building permits and may require an engineer\u2019s report\r\n- 120 days for completion, maximum 6 months\r\n- Projected income may be considered on a case-by-case basis when clients are looking to use the program to add a rental unit with a separate entrance.\r\n- Up to 3 draws can be processed on any amount over $40K. Request for draws to be established at the time of commitment.\r\n* Improvements >$20K: Appraisal/Inspection from a certified appraiser confirming all work has been completed\r\n* Improvements </=$20K: Satisfactory before/after photographs and paid invoices\r\n**Documentation and Advance of Funds**\r\n- Quotes for the improvements to be completed must be provided upfront for review.\r\n- If improvements are completed by the borrower(s), only the cost of materials will be considered. Inspection and paid receipts are required to advance improvement funds.\r\n- Applicable building/development permits must be provided (where applicable).\r\n- Any changes made post are subject to underwriting review. Changes must be supported to maintain a dollar-for-dollar value appreciation and authorized by Credit Management. \" (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Ontario)",
        "isAccepted": null
