        "id": 26,
        "policy": "New to Canada",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **A Side Accelerator**\r\n**New to Canada Program Overview**\r\n* The New to Canada Program under the Accelerator Mortgage suite is designed for recent immigrants purchasing their first home in Canada, often with limited or no domestic credit history.\r\n**Credit Score:**\r\n* Zero accepted (for newcomers without Canadian credit).\r\n* Insured: Minimum FICO\u00ae 640 per applicant.\r\n* Insurable: Minimum FICO\u00ae 680 per applicant.\r\n**Credit Verification Options:**\r\n* Borrowers must show credit responsibility through one of the following:\r\n* International credit report (Equifax or TransUnion) showing good credit; or\r\n* Two alternative credit sources with 12-month payment history, such as:\r\n* Rental payment history (with landlord letter + 12 months\u2019 bank statements)\r\n* Utility, phone, cable, or auto insurance bills (with provider letter or 12 months\u2019 statements)\r\n**Employment Requirements:**\r\n* At least 3 months full-time employment in Canada\r\n* Exceptions apply for corporate relocations.\r\n**Income:**\r\n* Standard employment and income verification applies.\r\n* Foreign income not accepted in qualification ratios.\r\n**Other Eligibility Criteria**\r\n* Must have immigrated to Canada within the last 5 years.\r\n* Must hold a valid work permit or permanent residency.\r\n* All debts held outside Canada must be included in qualification ratios.\r\n* Borrowers who are diplomats or foreign-appointed individuals are not eligible.\r\n* Borrowers must not be prohibited under the Prohibition on the Purchase of Residential Property by Non-Canadians Act.\r\n**Special note re Alternative Loans**\r\n* Home Trust will also review New to Canada scenarios in the alternative area . Discuss with your BDM (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Quebec)",
