        "policy": "Income - Salaried, Hourly, Contract, Part-Time, Bonus or Casual",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] * Marathon Mortgage Corp. will generally expect at least 2-years tenure with the same employer. When employment is less than 2 years with the same employer, generally the Underwriter will consider the application on a case-by-case basis. Where employment has been preferably in the same line of work, and/or the change of employment had occurred for reasons of self-improvement.\r\n**Letter Of Employment**\r\n* A Letter of Employment including a PDF version is generally acceptable form of income confirmation for most employment with the exception of those who work for a relative or who are on contract.\r\n* Letters signed by a relative or applicants who work for a family business must be treated as self employed and the applicant must provide the applicable documents\r\n* The letter needs to include gross base salary or hourly wage plus minimum guaranteed hours to be acceptable\r\n* Any bonus the applicant earns must be confirmed in the letter of employment and stated separately even if if it is not being used for qualification. If it is needed to qualifiy then guidelines around fluctuation income will apply\r\n* It should be on Letterhead, dated not earlier than 60 days\r\n* The contact name and title should be on the letter along with their signature\r\n* If the letter is handwritten it can not be used for confirmation of income\r\n* If not on letter head it can also not be used for confirmation\r\n**Salaried Income**\r\n* Salaried employees are to be employed for a minimum of two years (preferred), if less than two years, preferably in the same line of work, with no probation.\r\n* Salaried employees need to provide one of;\r\n* Curent Paystub\r\n* Current Letter of Employment (see above regarding required details)\r\n* 2 month direct deposit history\r\n* Salaried Employees need to also provide one of;\r\n* Most recent NOA\r\n* Previous Year End Pay stub\r\n* T4\r\n* Please note where a Letter of Employment and direct deposit or current paystub is provided then the secondary requirements of one of NOA etc are not required\r\n**Hourly Income (Full-Time with Guaranteed Hours)**\r\n* Where the hours and wages do not fluctuate follow the guidelines as noted above\r\n**Hourly Income (Part-Time with Non-Guaranteed Hours)**\r\n* Some applicants receive an income that fluctuates. For these applicants you will need to provide 2 documents that confirm historical annual income in different years. The average of these 2 historical years is used to service the request. A third document provides evidence employment is ongoing and current\r\n* Any two of the following are acceptable, NOA, Year End Paystub, T4\r\n* Will also need 1 of Letter of Employment, Direct Deposit, Pay Stub\r\n* An average of NOA etc is what is used.\r\n* If there is a variance of 20% on the most recent annual document then use the lower figure\r\n**Overtime and/or Bonus Income**\r\n* This would be treated like the fluctuating income above.\" (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
