        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **INVESTMENT INCOME**\r\nYou can utilize investment income to benefit your clients' mortgages! Here's how:\r\nWhen it\u2019s reasonably expected that a client will continue earning income from investments, the income from the previous year or the average income from the past two years can be applied to a mortgage. This is contingent upon verification of investment statements and receipt of income. *Capital Gains are not eligible.*\r\n*Due diligence to be completed to verify the continued reasonableness and sustainability of the income. Investments are not to be liquidated (i.e., down payments).*\r\n**RRSP/RRIF**\r\nIf a client retires and starts to withdraw from a RRSP or RRIF, their current income can be used without needing a 2-year history, provided that it can be reasonably expected to continue, and the investment balance can support annual withdrawals for at least 3 years\r\n**SUPPORTING DOCUMENTATION**\r\nSupporting documents must include investment statement(s) that state the client\u2019s name, investment company, account number, and balances. These statements must demonstrate the same or greater level of income sustainability and be dated no more than 60 days before the application.\r\nProof of income must be supported by NOAs (supported by T1 Generals), T5s, T4As, and T4RIFs from the most recent 2 years. (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
