        "policy": "New to Canada",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Purpose**\r\n* Purchase\r\n* Purchase Plus Improvements\r\n* Ports and Replacements\r\n**Eligibility**\r\n- **Non-Permanent Resident:** Foreign workers need a valid Canadian Employment Authorization Form (work permit), and their application must be referred and disclosed to the insurer. \r\n- **Permanent Resident:** Verification of landed immigrant status is required, and the borrower must have immigrated or relocated to Canada within the last 60 months. 3 months minimum full-time employment in Canada (borrowers transferred under a corporate relocation are exempt), and a minimum of 2 years of employment history is required.\r\n- Individuals with **diplomatic immunity** are NOT eligible.\r\n* High Ratio and Insurable ONLY\r\n* Up to 95% LTV High Ratio\r\n* Up to 80% LTV Insurable GDS/TDS: 39%/44% (all debts outside of Canada are to be included in the ratios)\r\n**Beacon Score**\r\n\u2022 Zero beacon or minimum beacon score of 650 for all applicants\r\n\u2022 GDS/TDS: 39%/44% (all debts outside of Canada are to be included in the ratios)\r\n**DownPayment**\r\n- Down payment is to be from own resources\r\n- Minimum 5% down payment may now be gifted from an immediate family member \r\n**Credit Requirements**\r\n- 90.01-95% LTV:\r\n - US or UK International to have a credit bureau demonstrating a strong credit profile OR\r\n - Two (2) alternative sources of credit demonstrating timely payments (no arrears) for the past 12 months (from a Canadian source). The two alternative sources required are:\r\n - Rental payment history confirmed via letter from landlord with supporting bank statements (Letter from landlord indicating the following is required: name of tenant, monthly rent, length of tenancy, payment history) AND\r\n - Hydro/utilities, telephone, cable, cell phone and auto insurance to be confirmed via letter from service provider or 12 months of billing statements\r\n - Up to 95% LTV for Purchase: 1-2 units\r\n- Up to 90% LTV:\r\n - Six (6) months bank statements from a recognized financial institution for borrowers\u2019 primary account OR A letter of reference from the borrower\u2019s recognized financial institution\r\n - No previous bankruptcies, foreclosures or mortgage delinquencies\r\n - Up to 90% LTV for Purchase: 3-4 units\r\n**Rate Qualification**\r\n- High Ratio: Greater of Contract Rate or Bank of Canada 5 year Benchmark rate\r\n- Insurable: Greater of Contract Rate +2% or Bank of Canada 5 year Benchmark Rate\r\n**Property Types**\r\n- Maximum 4 units, with 1 unit owner-occupied (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
