        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Overview**\r\n* RFA\u2019s Second Home Program is designed to help borrowers finance the purchase of a second home, particularly where the intention is:\r\n* To occupy both properties (main and second home) at different points during the year, or\r\n* Where the second property will be occupied by an immediate family member rent-free.\r\n* This makes it a good fit for clients looking to invest in a vacation home or provide housing for family members.\r\n**Property Eligibility Criteria**\r\n* If the second home is being classified as a vacation property, it must meet the following conditions to qualify for financing:\r\n* Permanent heat source\r\n* (This ensures year-round usability, especially in colder climates.)\r\n* Acceptable year-round water source\r\n* (Indicates reliability and access to water throughout the year.)\r\n* Permanent primary source of electricity\r\n* Note: Generators are not acceptable as the main electricity source.\r\n* Built for year-round occupancy\r\n* Must have year-round access via municipal, provincial, or territorial roads.\r\n* These conditions emphasize that the property must be livable throughout the year, not just seasonally accessible. (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
