        "policy": "Income - Professionals",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Overview**\r\n* The Projected Income for Physicians Program enables qualifying medical professionals to use projected future income (based on industry averages) to qualify for a mortgage, especially when their current income is lower than average earnings in their field.\r\n**Eligible Borrowers**\r\n* Medical Residents/Fellows: Currently enrolled in a recognized residency or fellowship in Canada.\r\n* Newly Practicing Physicians: Those who began working in a related field within the past 36 months.\r\n* Foreign-Trained Physicians: Must be licensed by a provincial college and be a Canadian citizen or permanent resident. Eligibility to use projected income extends to 36 months post-program completion.\r\n**Eligible Loan Purposes**\r\n* Loan Purposes: Purchase, Refinance, Switch\r\n**Loan Parameters**\r\n* Gross/Total Debt Service Ratios (GDSR/TDSR)\r\n* Standard ratios apply using projected income.\r\n* Student loans and lines of credit must be included in TDSR calculations.\r\n**Loan-to-Value (LTV) Ratios**\r\n* Insured Mortgages: Up to 90% (sliding scales apply)\r\n* Uninsured Mortgages:\r\n* 80% LTV if actual income \u2265 25% of projected income\r\n* 65% LTV if actual income < 25% of projected income\r\n* No exceptions; ScotiaLine\u00ae products are capped at 65% LTV\r\n* Scotia STEP\u00ae Program: Global limit is 80% of lending value\r\n**Documentation Requirements**\r\n* Depending on Applicant Type:\r\n* Residents/Fellows: Confirmation of enrolment, specialty, and current year.\r\n* Newly Practicing (Canada): Proof of program completion within the last 36 months.\r\n* Foreign-Trained: Proof of program completion and active provincial college registration.\r\n* Note: For first-year residents, if provincial registration isn\u2019t yet published, alternate documentation and verbal confirmation from the program provider is acceptable.\r\n**Down Payment Requirements**\r\n* Insured Mortgages: Minimum 10% (at least 5% from own resources)\r\n* Uninsured Mortgages: Minimum 20% (at least 10% from own resources)\r\n* Gifted Down Payments: Allowed\r\n**No Secondary Financing**\r\n* Not permitted on subject property\r\n**Income Verification Guidelines**\r\n* Projected Income:\r\n* Category Projected Income\r\n* 1st/2nd Year Residents $185,000\r\n* 3rd Year Residents $225,000\r\n* Family Medicine Residents (final year) $225,000\r\n* Other Final-Year Residents / New Physicians Use specialty chart\r\n* If not listed: Default = $225,000\r\n**Medical Specialties \u2013 Projected Income** \r\n* Cardiology: $359,000\r\n* Ophthalmology: $379,000\r\n* Most other specialties: $300,000\r\n* Family Medicine: $225,000\r\n* Gastroenterology: $309,000\r\n**Verification Sources**\r\n* Provincial college websites for verifying medical licenses are provided \r\n**Program Exclusions**\r\n* Mobile Homes\r\n* Progress Draw Mortgages\r\n* Certain specialized mortgage programs:\r\n* StartRight\r\n* Scotia Rental/Secondary Home Financing\r\n* On Reserve Lending\r\n* Renovation or Purchase Plus Improvements\r\n* Manufactured Homes\r\n**Projected Income for Dentists, Veterinarians, and Optometrists - Program Overview**\r\n* This program enables qualifying borrowers in the healthcare field (dentists, veterinarians, and optometrists) to use projected income rather than current earnings when applying for a mortgage. It targets:\r\n* Final-year students (residency, fellowship, or relevant study program)\r\n* Newly practicing professionals within:\r\n* 24 months for dentists\r\n* 12 months for veterinarians and optometrists\r\n**Eligibility Criteria**\r\n**Borrower Qualifications**\r\n* Must be in the final year of their study/residency program in Canada\r\n* Or newly practicing professionals who completed studies within the applicable time frames\r\n* Must be employed in a field related to their study\r\n* Applications with no income or unrelated field income are not accepted\r\n**Income Verification - Borrowers may use the following projected incomes to qualify**\r\n* Profession Projected Income\r\n* Dentist $175,000\r\n* Veterinary Medicine $86,000\r\n* Optometry $96,000\r\n* Standard income documentation is also required to verify actual earnings.\r\n**Eligible Loan Purposes**\r\n* Purchase\r\n* Refinance\r\n**Property Types**\r\n* Owner-occupied principal residence\r\n* Up to two units\r\n**Loan-to-Value (LTV) Ratios**\r\n* Insured: Up to 90% (with standard LTV sliding scales)\r\n* Uninsured:\r\n* Max 80% LTV if actual income is \u226525% of projected income\r\n* Max 65% LTV if actual income is <25% of projected income\r\n**Down Payment Requirements**\r\n* Insured: Minimum 10% (at least 5% from own resources)\r\n* Uninsured: Minimum 20% (at least 15% from own resources)\r\n* Gifted down payments are allowed\r\n**Documentation Requirements**\r\n* Depending on borrower status:\r\n* Final-Year Students:\r\n* Proof of enrollment showing current year in program\r\n* Optometry students: Must be enrolled at University of Waterloo or University of Montreal (no exceptions)\r\n* Newly Practicing:\r\n* Proof of program completion with date\r\n* Dentists: Doctor of Dental Surgery (Canada) within 24 months\r\n* Veterinarians: Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (Canada) within 12 months\r\n* Optometrists: Doctor of Optometry (University of Waterloo or Montreal) within 12 months. (Applies: National)",
