        "policy": "Purchase Plus Improvement & Refinance Plus Improvement",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **KEY FEATURES**\r\n* This program allows for qualified homebuyers who want to make cosmetic improvements to their newly purchased property within 120 days of taking possession (basement finishing, bathroom fixtures, kitchen cabinets/counters, flooring, new windows, detached garage).\r\n\u2022 The \u2018as-improved\u2019 value is used to determine the maximum loan amount, subject to loan-to-value (LTV) limitations. \r\n**Eligible Properties**\r\n* Uninsured: Owner-occupied properties: maximum of 2 units\r\n* Uninsured: Rental Properties\r\n* Uninsured: Scotia Secondary Home Financing Program\r\n* Type A & B properties: maximum 1 unit\r\n* Insured: Owner-occupied properties: maximum 4 units\r\n* Insured: Rental properties with maximum 80% LTV (one unit must be owner-occupied)\r\n* Insured: Scotia Secondary Home\u00ae Financing Program\r\n* Type A properties: maximum 4 units\r\n* Type B properties: maximum 1 unit\r\n**Eligible Loan Purposes**\r\n\u2022 Purchase only\r\n* Maximum Loan to Value (LTV) Ratio\r\n* (Mortgage default insurance fees and premiums may apply)\r\n* Standalone Mortgage\r\n* Uninsured 1-2 Units: 80% LTV\r\n* Insured 1-2 Units: 95% LTV\r\n* Insured 3-4 Units: 90% LTV\r\n**Scotia Total Equity\u00ae Plan (Scotia STEP\u00ae Program)**\r\n* Maximum Scotia STEP\u00ae Global Limit is 80% of lending value\r\n* One mortgage component only until mortgage is 100% complete and advanced\r\n**Amortization**\r\n* Up to 30 years for eligible applicants Maximum Number of Advances\r\n**Advances**\r\n\u2022 Maximum 2 advances, including property purchase, to be completed within 120 days of the first advance\r\n**Down Payment**\r\n* Down payment requirements are based on the \u2018as-improved\u2019 value of the property\r\n* Standard requirements apply\r\n**Appraisal Requirements for Uninsured Deals**\r\n* Full appraisal report, confirming both \u201cas-is\u201d and \u201cas-complete\u201d property values\r\n* All estimates and other supporting docs must be provided to appraiser to ensure the as-improved value is confirmed\r\n* An inspection must be ordered to ensure improvements are being completed prior to releasing the holdback\r\n**Maximum Value of Improvements**\r\n* Uninsured: Improvements cannot exceed 20% of the purchase price (\u2018as-is\u2019 property value).\r\n* Sagen or CG Insured: Improvements cannot exceed 20% of the as-is\u2019 property value\r\n* CMHC Insured: Improvements cannot exceed 10% of the \u2018as-improved\u2019 property lending value\r\n**Notes**\r\n* As-is\u2019 property value is the property lending value at time of purchase\r\n* As-improved\u2019 property value is equal to the lesser of the improved property value (as determined by the insurer), or\r\nthe \u2018as-is\u2019 property value plus the value of the improvements. (Value of improvements is based on the direct costs associated with the improvements).\r\n**Documentation Requirements**\r\n\u2022 Official cost estimates for the improvements, supported by suitable plans or diagrams\r\n\u2022 Copies of the building plans and sketches\r\n* A complete breakdown of construction costs with copies of the building contract or subcontractor estimates\r\n**Exclusions**\r\n* Improvements to correct deficiencies, make the home livable, complete an addition, or repair structural concerns\r\n* When the value of improvements exceeds established program limits or falls under the threshold with two mortgage\r\ncomponents\r\n* Scotiabank StartRight\u00ae for Temporary and Permanent Residents\r\n* The Long and Short\u00ae Mortgage\r\n* Refinances\r\n* Note to Brokers: Finder fee will be issued once improvements are complete (or no longer required) (Applies: National)",
