        "id": 55,
        "policy": "HELOC Products - General",
        "description": "* Please note that the Scotia Bank STEP is not automatically a re-advance-able account. If you want the STEP to be re-advance-able, you must request STEP ALI(Auto Limit Increase) in the deal notes. Otherwise the HELOC will not grow (re-advance) as the mortgage is paid down.\r\n* ONLY Two Borrowers allowed on STEP \r\n* STEP can be used for Insured files if client wishes to have fixed & variable portions up to 95%. Global limit will be set at 80%\r\n* Revolving portions amortized over 25 years\r\n* on refinanced when using Title Insurance to close no additional cost for ALI. When using a lawyer there will be additional cost to the client to have title insurance.\r\n* client can attend branch at maturity to change the restructuring of the STEP to all revolving at no charge and they do not need to re-qualify if no other changes.\r\n* Fixed Portions can be amortized up to 30 years\r\n* auto re advance, up to 6 parts\r\n* Discretionary Pricing for ScotiaLine limits between $10,000 and $24,900: no discretion available \r\n* For limits between $25,000 and $49,900: 25 bps discretion available \r\n* For limits of $50,000 or more: 50 bps discretion available \r\n* Please note the that minimum Secured Loc is now $10,000.00\r\nthis is discretionary pricing and is not updated as such on the rate sheet \r\n* No discount on Secured Loc for Rental properties\r\n**ILA**\r\nEffective immediately, if ILA is required for a refinance that is closing through the Instant Funding Program ( i.e is NOT solicitor facilitated) , the ILA will have to be obtained before closing. You will be responsible for providing the ILA form to your client and they will have to complete it and return it as soon as possible. The form is located on the Scotia Mortgage Authority website under Tools and Resources- Forms- Certificate of Independent Legal Advice.\r\nThere will be a specific condition in the commitment letter to inform you when ILA is required and it will be outstanding on the website until the ILA certificate is returned to underwriter (BRM)\r\nPlease note, that the file will not be instructed to FCT/FNF UNTIL the ILA form is completed.\r\nILA is mandatory when the subject property is a principal residence that is being registered in one spouses name and is A STEP. Non-step files do not require ILA however we do reserve the right to ask for ILA on any file we deem necessary.\r\n**Note** \r\n* For all new and eligible existing STEPs, the STEP Global Limit will gradually reduce to 65% LTV over a 25-year\r\nperiod, effective November 1st, 2023. The reduction will be applied in equal monthly adjustments on the fifth calendar day of each month. Customers will continue to be able to refinance to increase the STEP Global Limit up to 80% LTV. Once refinanced, the 25-year monthly reduction of the STEP Global Limit to 65% LTV would restart (Applies: National)",
