        "policy": "Property Type",
        "description": "* No former Grow Ops for Broker Channel. Refer to Branch for consideration\r\n* Permanent foundation and installed below the frost line\r\n* Complete, structurally sound with no major repairs or updating required\r\n* Central heating, potable water supply and sanitary sewer, septic system or holding tank\r\n* Remaining economic life of at least 5 years greater than the amortization period.\r\n* Zoned and used as residential, rural or seasonal. Mixed use, short-term rentals or rental pooling are not eligible\r\n* Year-round access on reasonable quality public roads\r\n* Good market appeal, within price range for area and no adverse influences/neighborhood nuisances\r\n**Guidelines for Cottage and Leisure Homes:**\r\n* The value of docks, boathouses, bunkies can be included in property value Cottage\r\n**Cottage Properties can be divided into two types:**\r\n* Type A: the criteria for Residential Properties apply\r\n* Type B: central heating not required; seasonal road access (i.e. road is not plowed) is acceptable For more details, see Scotia Secondary Home\u00ae Financing Program\r\n**Wood Basements For PWF houses built in 1995 or later:**\r\n* No special requirements apply.\r\n* For PWF houses built before 1995:\r\n* Obtain a full appraisal report with instructions to pay particular attention to the condition of the foundation. The appraiser is to document any existing or potential problems discovered in the report.\r\n* If the appraiser finds problems with the foundation, an engineer\u2019s certificate is required.\r\n* Review Multiple PIDs/LOTS with your BRM. (Applies: National)",
