        "id": 28,
        "policy": "Purchase Plus Improvement & Refinance Plus Improvement",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Loan Purpose**\r\n* With Strive\u2019s Purchase Plus Improvements (PPI) Program, borrowers can include improvement costs within their mortgage, allowing clients to transform their new property immediately after taking possession. * Regardless of the scale of the project, this program empowers clients to bring their vision to life and ensures their new property reflects their preferences.\r\n**Maximum Loan-to-Value (LTV)** \r\n* Insured:\r\n* 95% for 1\u20132 units\r\n* 90% for 3\u20134 units (must have municipal zoning with self-contained units)\r\n* Insurable: \u2264 80%\r\n* LTV is based on the \u201cas improved\u201d value of the property.\r\n**Property Type**\r\n* Maximum 4 units, with 1 unit owner-occupied\r\n* Property value must be less than $1,000,000\r\n**Down Payment**\r\n* Minimum 5% required, based on the \u201cas improved\u201d value of the property.\r\n**Eligible Products**\r\n* Stated Income\r\n* New to Canada\r\n* Vacation / Secondary Home\r\n* Investment Property\r\n* Borrowed Down\r\n**Purchase Plus Improvements (PPI) Highlights**\r\n* PPI amounts range from $5,000 to $150,000; exceptions beyond this amount may be considered.\r\n* Improvements must support dollar-for-dollar ($1 for $1) value appreciation.\r\n* Structural improvements may require applicable development and building permits and may also require an engineer\u2019s report.\r\n* Improvements must be completed within 120 days, with a maximum of 6 months.\r\n* Projected income may be considered on a case-by-case basis when the program is used to add a rental unit with a separate entrance.\r\n**Draws for Improvements**\r\n* Up to 3 draws can be processed on any amount over $40,000.\r\n* Minimum draw amount: $5,000.\r\n* Requests for multiple draws must be established at the time of commitment. If not requested at commitment, only one draw is permitted.\r\n* Improvements under $20,000: Paid invoices and before/after photos acceptable.\r\n* Improvements under $40,000: Inspection required.\r\n* Improvements over $40,000: Inspection and paid invoices required. If invoices are unpaid, Strive may direct funds directly to contractor(s) via solicitor instructions.\r\n**Documentation and Advance of Funds**\r\n* Quotes for all improvements must be provided upfront for review.\r\n* If improvements are completed by the borrower(s), only the cost of materials will be considered. Paid receipts and an inspection are required to advance funds.\r\n* If improvements include the addition of a rental unit, an inspection is required regardless of renovation amount.\r\n* Any changes made post-funding from the approved work outlined in Strive\u2019s mortgage commitment are subject to underwriting review. Changes must continue to support dollar-for-dollar value appreciation and be authorized by Credit Management. If changes are deemed not to support value, the equivalent holdback amount will be applied to the principal balance of the mortgage.\r\n**Strive Refinance Plus Improvements Program**\r\n* Strive\u2019s Refinance Plus Improvements program is designed to help homeowners increase the value and utility of their properties by refinancing to add legal rental suites. This initiative aligns with efforts to support diverse housing options within communities.\r\n**Loan Purpose**\r\n* Objective: Add a legal, self-contained rental suite to an existing owner-occupied property.\r\n**Key Borrower Qualifications**\r\n* Must already own and occupy the property.\r\n* Must intend to construct additional legal suites that:\r\n* Are not used for short-term rentals.\r\n* Include at least one unit occupied rent-free by the borrower or a related person.\r\n**Must provide:**\r\n* Fair market rent appraisal to confirm projected rental income.\r\n* 25% of total improvement amount in confirmed liquid assets.\r\n* Standard income documentation per insurer guidelines.\r\n**Program Requirements**\r\n* New suite must be:\r\n* Legal and fully self-contained.\r\n* Zoning compliant under municipal bylaws.\r\n**Documentation needed:**\r\n* Building permit (or equivalent) on file at initial funding.\r\n* Occupancy certificate confirming legality prior to final draw release.\r\n* Statutory declarations confirming:\r\n* The suite won\u2019t be used for short-term rentals.\r\n* Final draw is conditional on suite legality.\r\n**Mortgage Details**\r\n* Maximum LTV: 90% of the \"as improved value\", up to $2,000,000 (subject to sliding scale).\r\n* Value Basis: Current value + cost of improvements.\r\n* May include consolidation of existing debt if secured by standard/collateral charge.\r\n**Terms and Amortization**\r\n* Product Types:\r\n* Fixed-rate: 1\u20135 years\r\n* ARM: 5 years\r\n* Amortization Options:\r\n* Maintain existing amortization with same insurer.\r\n* Blend existing + new period.\r\n* New insured amortization up to 30 years.\r\n**Insurance Premium:**\r\n* Existing rates apply.\r\n* Additional 20 bps for amortizations >25 years.\r\n* Qualifying Rate:\r\n* Higher of contract rate + 2% or BoC 5-year benchmark.\r\n**Ineligible Uses**\r\n* Purchase transactions\r\n* Mortgage transfers. (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Northwest Territories, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan, Yukon)",
