        "id": 11,
        "policy": "Income - Disability",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] Social assistance benefits are generally not accepted as qualifying income for debt servicing. However, provincial government disability support payments, such as the Ontario Disability Support Program (ODSP), are permissible if the benefits are confirmed to be permanent.\r\n**Required Documentation:**\r\nTo verify permanent disability support income, provide one of the following sets of documents:\r\n1. **Current Pay Stub or Direct Deposit Proof**: Submit a recent pay stub or evidence of a direct deposit reflecting the disability support payment.\r\n2. **Confirmation of Permanent Benefit**: Provide a letter from the relevant provincial authority confirming the permanency of the benefit.\r\n3. **Tax Documentation**: Supply the most recent two years of T1 General tax returns, specifically highlighting Line 14500, which pertains to social assistance payments.\r\n4. **Statement of Benefits**: Present the most recent two years of T5007 forms, which detail the Statement of Benefits received.\r\nThese documents collectively establish the stability and permanence of the disability support income, ensuring it meets the criteria for debt servicing considerations. (Applies: National)",
