        "policy": "Rentals - Fair Market Rents",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **For Purchase Applications Only**\r\n- Up to 80% LTV where market rent is being used, up to a maximum of 2 rental properties \r\n**For Refinance Applications**\r\n- Market rent can be used where LTV is \u2264 65%. \r\n- Exceptions may be considered for LTV > 65% for customers with strong net worth and a deep TD relationship and must be escalated to RRMCG\r\n**Market Rent**\r\n- For purchase and refinance transactions where the property is not rented, market rent can be used in lieu of lease agreements for qualification purposes.\r\n- For purchase applications \u2013 Maximum 80% LTV where market rent is being used to a maximum of 2 rental properties\r\n- For refinance applications \u2013 Maximum 65% LTV where market rent is used to substantiate rental income. Exceptions may be considered for LTV > 65% for customers with strong credit history and net worth\r\n- Market rent assessment must be provided by the appraiser and included in the appraisal comments\r\n- The lowest market rent in the report is to be used\r\n- Where property is an owner-occupied single-family dwelling and has more than one unit (i.e., property with main floor unit and two finished basement units), the unit(s) with the lowest market rent(s) must be used for debt service calculations (regardless of which unit will be rented). Note: only market rents for finished/rentable units are eligible.\r\n- If a customer is turning their existing owner-occupied property into a rental property and purchasing a new owner-occupied, market rents could be used to support this\r\nrental property. Maximum LTV is 65%.\r\n**Assignment of Rent**\r\n- All provinces except British Columbia:\r\n - Assignment of Rents is included in the Standard Charge Terms - a separate Assignment of Rents document is not required.\r\n- British Columbia:\r\n - Assignment of Rents is included in the Standard Charge Terms - a separate Assignment of Rents document is not required. However, the Supplier must advise the solicitor to register the mortgage with this clause outlined in the registration in order for the Assignment of Rents clause to be valid (Applies: National)",
