        "id": 32,
        "policy": "Second Homes / Family Plan",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Overview**\r\n- Available for high-ratio financing through Sagen/Canada Guaranty for second homes that are either owner-occupied or occupied by the mortgagor\u2019s immediate family member on a rent-free basis.\r\n- Maximum purchase price/lending value for high-ratio deals is less than $1 million, with a maximum of one unit.\r\n- *Note:* Conventional applications for second owner-occupied properties follow the regular conventional application policy.\r\n**Guidelines**\r\n**Eligible Product**\r\n- Conventional and Insured Mortgage\r\n- Fixed Rate\r\n- Closed VIRM\r\n- Conventional TD Home Equity FlexLine\r\n**Purpose**\r\n- Purchase and Refinance (Single Advance)\r\n- Purchase plus Improvements\r\n- Refer to 1.5.2\r\n**Property**\r\n- Single Unit Properties:\r\n - Owner-occupied\r\n - Occupied by an immediate family member on a rent-free basis\r\n**Ineligible Product**\r\n- All product types not listed under Eligible\r\n**Purpose**\r\n- Insured refinance\r\n- Non-residents for insured applications\r\n- Temporary residents\r\n- Refinance plus Improvements (unless Default Insured)\r\n**Property**\r\n- Rental properties\r\n**Property Criteria**\r\n- Must meet standard TD property criteria, including:\r\n - Year-round road access\r\n - Fully serviced with municipal water and sanitary sewers, well and septic tank, or a combination\r\n - Winterized with a permanent heat source\r\n - Located in Canada\r\n - Estimated remaining economic life of at least 25 years\r\n**Borrower Eligibility**\r\n- Standard credit qualification criteria apply\r\n- No R3s (missed payments) in the last 24 months\r\n- No prior bankruptcies or judgments\r\n- No third-party guarantors (spousal guarantor is acceptable)\r\n- TDS must include servicing costs for both properties, such as taxes, heat, condo fees, and/or HOA fees, if applicable, for the principal residence\r\n**Down Payment Restriction**\r\n- **Conventional:** Standard down payment criteria apply.\r\n- **Insured:** \r\n - Gifted down payment from immediate family members is acceptable. An immediate family member includes a father, mother, child, brother, sister, grandparent, legal guardian, or legal dependent.\r\n - Default Insured Purchase: 95%\r\n**Amortization**\r\n- **Insured:**\r\n - Up to 30 years for First-Time Home Buyers purchasing a newly constructed home.*\r\n - *Note:* Ownership of a primary residence is not required to qualify for a second home. The primary residence may be rented, or the borrower may live with relatives. Borrowers can qualify as First-Time Home Buyers for a second home under these conditions (see section 9.1 Default Insurance for qualifying criteria).\r\n - Up to 25 years for all other applications.\r\n- **Conventional:** Maximum of 30 years.\r\n**Maximum Loan Amount**\r\n- **Conventional:** No maximum.\r\n- **Insured:** \r\n - $700,000 for Toronto, Calgary, and Vancouver\r\n - $600,000 for the rest of Canada (Applies: National)",
