        "id": 62,
        "policy": "Lawyer",
        "description": "**Remote Signing with First Canadian Title (FCT)**\r\n**Policy Overview**\r\n* Effective immediately, TD allows for remote signing of mortgage documents via FCT, provided the following identification and title insurance requirements are met.\r\n**Identification Requirements**\r\n* To comply with TD's standards\u2014especially under remote signing conditions\u2014FCT must verify client identity using:\r\n* Primary ID:\r\n* One authentic, valid, unexpired Canadian government-issued photo ID\r\n* Must include the customer\u2019s full name and date of birth\r\n* Examples: Driver\u2019s license, passport, permanent resident card\r\n* Secondary ID (Choose one):\r\n* A second Canadian government-issued ID that is different from the first or\r\n* A recent (within 60 days) Canadian financial institution statement (excluding TD), showing:\r\n* Customer\u2019s full name\r\n* Customer\u2019s residential address. (Applies: National)",
