        "id": 88,
        "policy": "Submission Tips & Underwriting Assistance",
        "description": "Anti-Money Laundering Legislation requires TD know who the customer is and, complete Know Your Customer (KYC) (AML) information anytime a new mortgage product is offered\r\n**Resubmission**\r\n* A broker will be asked to resubmit application \r\n* When there is a co-applicant/guarantor added to the application \r\n* When there is an applicant being removed from the application \r\n* Instance where pre-approval becomes associated with a particular property \r\n* When a new bureau is needed to re-adjudicate a credit request \r\n* When the name of applicant changes, not however for a correction Bob Smith is changed to Robert Smith \r\n* When a broker is making substantial changes to the application\r\n* Yes, TransUnion accepted \r\n**Pricing**\r\n* On Live/Committed deals only, in order to consider approvals for additional discretionary pricing, complete the Rate Exception Request Form you received from your BDM\r\n**Leading Practices for Underwriting**\r\n* Document Compliance. Collect and consolidate a complete document package into one email to help reduce email volumes to TDMS.\r\n* First Time Right. Validate application details against supporting documentation to avoid any 'back and forth' and use submission comments to tell your customer's full story. Your RSM/ISM is available to answer any policy or submission questions, prior to sending the file.\r\n* Time-sensitive Deals. Discuss time-sensitive applications with your RSM/ISM prior to submission to identify deals that may be at risk due to turn-around times.\r\n* TDMS Automated Replies. Automated email replies have been enabled at TDMS to confirm receipt of your email and provide information to help you redirect inquiries. This will allow Underwriters to increase their focus on adjudication and document compliance. Please note, at this time there is no fixed response time at TDMS and they will reply to emails on a best-effort basis.\r\n* Deal Status Updates. Use support protocols in place for deal status updates. Note: During this time, we ask that you manage expectations with your customers:\r\n * Refer to www.tdmortgagesolutions.com.\r\n * Speak with your RSM/ISM who has received enhanced system training to further support you with application information and status updates.\r\n* Deal Escalations. To appeal a decision on an application, you may escalate to your RSM/ISM or Broker Owner to review application details prior to resubmission.\r\n* TD Policy Inquiries. Speak with your RSM/ISM or refer to the Broker Information Kit (BIK) for policy inquiries before submitting your deal.\r\n**SignUp**\r\n- TD is individual unless you are on a team\r\n**Use the below Template in every TD Home Equity FlexLine submission request with accurate information confirmed from clients**\r\n* TD Home Equity FlexLine Template:\r\n* Original Plan Limit (up to 80% LTV) =\r\n* Credit Limit (up to 65% LTV and minimum of $20,000) =\r\n* Term Portion Amount (if applicable, minimum of $5000 and max of Plan limit) =\r\n* Amount to be advanced from Revolving Portion (in addition to Term Portion Amount) = (Applies: National)",
