        "id": 89,
        "policy": "Switch Transfer - General Information Standard Charge",
        "description": "* TD accepts transfers of conventional (non-collateral) mortgages from the below listed financial institutions:- Bank of Montreal- Bank of Nova Scotia- CIBC- Canadian Western Bank- First National -Laurentian Bank- National Bank- Royal Bank- Life Insurance Companies\r\n* Standard Income Confirmation Required \r\n* Mortgage Approval is subject to receipt of a Mortgage Statement for Assignment Purposes that confirms the mortgage is up-to-date and no arrears exists\r\n* Insured mortgages do not require an appraisal provided the mortgage is set up as an insured mortgage using the original insurer Reference Number\r\n* Mortgage transfers will be registered as a standard charge.\r\n* Transfers not acceptable if:\r\n * Private\r\n * Collateral mtg\r\n * no blended monthly P&I\r\n * non-assignable\r\n * non-tranf/clause in mortgage doc or standard charge terms\r\n**Switches of previous owner occupied into a rental not allowed. Would need to be a refinance as assignment of rents not allowed** (Applies: National)",
