        "policy": "Types of Financing",
        "description": "**Residential Financing**\r\n* Conventional Mortgages \u2013 For borrowers with a down payment of at least 20%, available in fixed and variable interest rate options.\r\n* High-Ratio Insured Mortgages \u2013 For clients with less than 20% down payment, requiring mortgage default insurance.\r\n* Home Equity Lines of Credit (HELOC) \u2013 Flexible, revolving credit secured by the home\u2019s equity, allowing access to funds as needed.\r\n* Newcomer and Non-Resident Programs \u2013 Tailored products for individuals new to Canada or living abroad but purchasing property in Canada.\r\n* Self-Employed Programs \u2013 Designed for borrowers with non-traditional income verification.\r\n* Purchase Plus Improvements \u2013 Financing that includes funds for home upgrades or renovations at the time of purchase. (Applies: National)",
