        "id": 24,
        "policy": "Rentals - Income",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Subject Rental Income**\r\n* Usage Policy\r\n* 90% of gross rental income can be added back to income for qualification.\r\n* Deductions Required:\r\n* Deduct:\r\n* Heat\r\n* Property taxes\r\n* Condo fees\r\n* Association fees, if applicable\r\n* Primary Residence with Rental Unit:\r\n* Still use 90% rental addback\r\n* No expenses (e.g., heat or taxes) are deducted if borrower pays them\r\n* Rental unit must be self-contained with a private entrance\r\n**Non-Subject Rental Income**\r\n* Usage Policy:\r\n* WealthONE applies a 90% rental offset approach:\r\n* Surplus is added to income\r\n* Shortfall is added to liabilities\r\n**Required Documentation**\r\n**Subject Rentals**\r\n* Market rent from appraisal\r\nOR\r\n* Lease agreement + supporting:\r\n* Bank statements or\r\n* Cancelled cheques\r\n* Most recent 2 years of FULL T1s\r\n* Articles of Incorporation (if property held in HoldCo)\r\n**Non-Subject Rentals:**\r\n* Flexible documentation:\r\n* Lease agreements\r\n* 2-year T1s\r\n* Rental worksheet\r\n* Tenant Acknowledgment Forms, if requested\r\n* Mortgage statements & property tax statements\r\n* Bank statements (to support expired leases). (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
