        "id": 37,
        "policy": "Condos",
        "description": "**Minimum Square Footage**\r\n* Condos must be at least: 375 sq ft\r\n**Condo LTV Limits Based on Location and Use**\r\n* WealthONE applies stricter LTV limits to condos than to non-condo properties. These vary by both location and occupancy type:\r\n* Greater Metropolitan Areas (500K+ population):\r\n* Up to 75% LTV for condo rentals\r\n* (By contrast: 80% LTV for owner-occupied and non-condo rentals)\r\n* Minor Urban Centres (50K\u2013499K population):\r\n* Up to 70% LTV for condo rentals\r\n* (Versus 75% for owner-occupied and non-condo rentals)\r\n* Rural Communities (<50K population):\r\n* Up to 65% LTV (same as other properties in rural areas)\r\n**Sliding Scale LTV for High-Value Condos**\r\n* For condo rentals:\r\n* Max 75% LTV on the first $1.5MM, then 50% LTV on the balance\r\n**Hotel Condos**\r\n* Hotel condominiums are acceptable, but only if located in the residence section\r\n**Restrictions on Condo Rentals**\r\n* Short-term rentals are not allowed under any circumstances. This includes:\r\n* Airbnb\r\n* Bed & Breakfasts\r\n* Student rentals\r\n* Rooming houses. (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
