        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **General Information**\r\n* Homeowners who would like to switch or transfer their Insured mortgage from an existing lender over to Manulife Bank\r\n* The minimum borrowing amount is $100,000\r\n* Closing services by First Canadian Title (FCT) or Fidelity National Financial (FNF), closing services are paid for by Manulife Bank at no cost to the borrower.\r\n* No appraisal required as the deal is already insured\r\n* prepayment privileges: Lump\u2011sum payment(s) up to 20% of the original mortgage amount, annually. Increase regular mortgage payments by up to 25% annually.\r\n* All other credit, income and documentation requirements are as per usual and based on the individual deal\r\n**Submitting Applications**\r\n\u2022 Submit the deal to Manulife Bank as a Manulife Bank \u2018Select\u2019 product and application purpose set as \u201cSwitch or Transfer\u201d.\r\n\u2022 If any prepayment penalties, or fees are being capitalized to the mortgage (Up to $3,000), this amount must be included in the application loan amount.\r\n\u2022 The following information is to be submitted with the application via notes:\r\n\u2022 Original or existing insurer reference number must be provided\r\n\u2022 Name of the insurer (CMHC, GE, or Canada Guaranty) Insurer account number\r\n\u2022 Previous insured mortgage advance date\r\n\u2022 Previous value or purchase price (should also be entered as the value in the deal submission)\r\n\u2022 Original and remaining amortization (Remaining amortization should also be entered as the amortization being requested for the deal)\r\n\u2022 The original loan amount + the premium amount\r\n**Special Note**\r\n* Insured lender switch the MQR does not need to be used. Instead, the file can be qualified using the customer\u2019s contract rate. This only applies to files that currently have default insurance, the default insurance is remaining in place, the mortgage is being ported as is with the only change being a change in FI. The same criteria of no more than $3,000 can be added to the mortgage still applies (Applies: National)",
