        "id": 35,
        "policy": "Appraisals",
        "description": "## Appraisal Requirements \u2013 Manulife Bank\r\n### A Full Appraisal is Required When:\r\n* The property has two or more units and the LTV is greater than 65%.\r\n* The credit amount requested exceeds $1,000,000.\r\n* The property is considered specialty use, including farms, or more than 20% of the property is used for commercial purposes.\r\n* The property is more than five acres.\r\n* The property is not or will not be owner occupied.\r\n* The property is a modular home (must be affixed to a concrete foundation).\r\n* The property is a condominium with known issues, including but not limited to building envelope or water leakage concerns.\r\n* There is an indication or suspicion of environmental issues or potential health hazards. If confirmed by the appraisal, a Phase I Environmental Site Assessment is required.\r\n* The property is a new construction/home build (except under the High Ratio Program). A progress inspection confirming at least 95% completion is required prior to funding.\r\n* The property is being sold under a private sale agreement.\r\n* The property is located in a Single Resource Industry Community.\r\n* The property is located in a rural area (postal code with \"0\" as the second character) or is not located in an approved lending area for automated valuation.\r\n* The property has a coach/carriage house or laneway building. These units must be legal, comply with municipal requirements, and contain a minimum of 500 square feet.\r\nWhere a full appraisal is required, the condition will be identified in the mortgage commitment. Appraisals must be ordered through one of Manulife Bank's approved appraisal management companies.\r\n---\r\n## Automated Valuation (AVM)\r\nAn automated valuation may be used when:\r\n* The property is an owner-occupied single-family dwelling on five acres or less.\r\n* The property is an owner-occupied two- to four-unit residential dwelling with a proposed LTV of 65% or less.\r\n* None of the conditions requiring a full appraisal apply.\r\nA full appraisal is required if:\r\n* An automated valuation is unavailable; or\r\n* The applicant disputes the automated valuation.\r\nUnderwriters may request a full appraisal whenever deemed necessary. (Applies: National)",
