        "id": 59,
        "policy": "Maximum or Minimum Amounts",
        "description": "**Minimum and Maximum Mortgage Amounts**\r\n* Minimum Loan Amounts\r\n* $100,000 minimum for:\r\n* Manulife Bank Select High-Ratio Program\r\n* Manulife Bank Select Conventional Insurable Program\r\n* (Applies to first-position accounts only)\r\n**Maximum Loan Amounts**\r\n* Manulife One: Up to $3,000,000\r\n* Manulife Bank Select: Up to $1,000,000\r\n**Exceptions**\r\n* For Manulife One, the insured property value cap of $1,000,000 may be exceeded if the mortgage being refinanced was funded prior to November 30, 2016 (i.e. before insurer policy changes took effect). This exception allows such mortgages to still be treated as \"standard insured\" under legacy rules.\r\n**Insured Mortgages & 30-Year Amortization**\r\n* The maximum mortgage amount for an insured property is $1,375,000.\r\n* This is based on a $1.5M purchase price, assuming the borrower provides the minimum required down payment per the insurer\u2019s guidelines.\r\n* Only applies to properties eligible for default insurance and subject to insurer maximums.\r\n**Loan-to-Value (LTV) Limits**\r\n* Conventional Insurable Program: Maximum 80% LTV. (Applies: National)",
