        "policy": "Personal Tax/ CRA Arrears",
        "description": "## Income Tax Arrears \u2013 Manulife Bank\r\n* Personal income taxes owing for any tax year should be current and paid prior to mortgage funding.\r\n* Outstanding tax balances must be verified using the most current Notice of Assessment (NOA).\r\n* In Quebec, both the federal and provincial NOAs must be reviewed.\r\n* Evidence that outstanding taxes have been paid may be provided through:\r\n * A bank statement showing the payment;\r\n * A copy of the cleared cheque; or\r\n * Confirmation from the applicable taxation authority.\r\n* At the discretion of the underwriter, an exception may be granted where the borrower has the capacity and willingness to satisfy the outstanding tax arrears.\r\n* Where an exception is granted, GDS/TDS ratios must remain within applicable program limits. (Applies: National)",
