        "policy": "Switch Transfer - General Information Standard Charge",
        "description": "* Target Market Homeowners who would like to switch/transfer their Insured mortgage from an existing lender over to \r\nManulife Bank \r\n* Loan to value (LTV) Up to 95% single detached home, townhouse, condominium or duplex \r\n* Up to 90% triplex or fourplex \r\n* Minimum borrowing limit \u2022 $100,000 \r\n* First position accounts only Preferred lending areas British Columbia, Alberta, Saskatchewan, Manitoba, Ontario, Quebec and Atlantic provinces Acceptable properties \r\n* Owner occupied single family dwelling (includes detached home, townhouse or condominium), duplex, \r\ntriplex and fourplex. \r\n* Property must be residentially\u2010zoned and utilized. \r\n* In\u2010law apartments permitted.\r\n* Maximum amortization Lesser of 25 years or actual remaining amortization \r\n**The following information is to be submitted with the application via notes**\r\n* Original/existing insurer reference number must be provided \r\n* Name of the insurer (CMHC, GE or Canada Guaranty) \r\n* Insurer account number \r\n* Previous insured mortgage advance date \r\n* Previous value or purchase price (should also be entered as the value in the deal submission) \r\n* Original and remaining amortization (Remaining amortization should also be entered as the amortization being requested for the deal) \r\n* The original loan amount + the premium amount \r\n* A new collateral charge will be registered for all Insured Lender Switches.\r\n**Special Note**\r\n* Insured lender switch the MQR does not need to be used. Instead, the file can be qualified using the customer\u2019s contract rate. This only applies to files that currently have default insurance, the default insurance is remaining in place, the mortgage is being ported as is with the only change being a change in FI. The same criteria of no more than $3,000 can be added to the mortgage still applies (Applies: National)",
