        "id": 26,
        "policy": "New to Canada",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] The MCAP New To Canada Program makes it possible for individuals relocating to Canada to purchase a home sooner with as little as 5% down. Through this program, MCAP helps new Canadians purchase their first home, build equity, and become economically established in Canada. Financing is available to borrowers with permanent and non-permanent residence status where there is limited Canadian credit history and where foreign credit bureaus may not be available\r\n**Purpose**\r\n* Purchases\r\n* Purchase Plus Improvements\r\n* Ports and Replacements\r\n(Currently not available in Quebec)\r\n**Borrower Eligibility**\r\n* Non-Permanent Residents: Foreign workers with valid Canadian employment authorization (Work Permit) in compliance with the Prohibition on the Purchase of Residential Property by Non-Canadians Act.\r\n* Permanent Residents: Verification of landed immigrant (permanent resident) status is required.\r\n* Minimum 2 years employment history required.\r\n* Individuals with diplomatic immunity are not eligible\r\n**Purchase Price**\r\n* Insured: Maximum $1,499,999\r\n* Insurable: Maximum $999,999\r\n**Loan-to-Value (LTV)**\r\n* High Ratio and Insurable only\r\n* Up to 95% LTV High Ratio (maximum 90% LTV for 3\u20134 units)\r\n* Up to 80% LTV Insurable\r\n**Beacon Scores**\r\n* Minimum of 0 or 600+ (Scores of 1\u2013599 are NOT eligible.)\u201d\r\n* Borrowers without Canadian credit history must comply with Alternative Sources of Credit requirements\r\n**Alternative Sources of Credit Requirements**\r\n* Borrowers must meet one of the following:\r\n* Option 1: US, UK, Australia or New Zealand International credit bureau demonstrating a strong credit profile\r\n* Option 2: Two Canadian alternative sources demonstrating 12 months of on-time payments (e.g., rental history + utilities/phone/insurance)\r\n* Option 3:\r\n* LTV > 90%: 12 months verifiable bank statements from a recognized Canadian FI or FI from the country of origin\r\n* LTV \u2264 90%: 6 months bank statements from a recognized FI for borrower\u2019s primary account\r\n* Option 4: Letter of reference from borrower\u2019s recognized financial institution\r\n**Amortization**\r\n* Minimum 5 years\r\n* Maximum 25 years\r\n* 30 years permitted for insured loans if:\r\n* Property is owner-occupied (or occupied by an immediate family member rent-free) and\r\n* One borrower is a First-Time Homebuyer or property is new construction\r\n**Acceptable Forms of Identification**\r\n* Each Borrower, Guarantor, and Signatory must present:\r\n* One piece of Primary ID and one piece of Secondary ID, OR\r\n* Two pieces of Primary ID\r\n* All ID must be original, valid, legible, and in good condition. Each individual must be physically present when identity is verified\r\n**Primary Identification**\r\n* Employee identity card with photo from a recognized employer\r\n* Signed ABM or client card (Canadian Payments Association member)\r\n* Signed credit card (Canadian Payments Association member)\r\n* CNIB card with photo\r\n* Canadian birth certificate\r\n* SIN card (Government of Canada)\r\n* Certificate of Canadian Citizenship\r\n* Citizenship & Immigration Form IMM1000 or IMM1442\r\n**Secondary Identification**\r\n* Valid Canadian driver\u2019s licence\r\n* Current Canadian Passport\r\n* Nexus card\r\n* Federally issued Firearms Licence\r\n* Certificate of Canadian Citizenship (with photo) or Certification of Naturalization (with photo)\r\n* Federally issued Permanent Resident Card\r\n* Certificate of Indian Status (Government of Canada)\r\n* Provincial Health Insurance Card (with photo)\u00b9\r\n* Provincial Government-issued Photo ID Card, or other provincial/territorial government-issued card with photo & signature\r\n* In Ontario, Manitoba, Nova Scotia, and Prince Edward Island, the Health Card is not acceptable. Another Primary ID must be provided\r\n. (Applies: National)",
