        "id": 69,
        "policy": "Pre Approvals & Rate Holds",
        "description": "**Adjudication:** Some submissions may auto-decline, and you will receive a system response explaining the reason. This allows you to make corrections if possible and resubmit the application. If you are uncertain about the auto-decline reason, please contact your Regional Business Manager.\r\n**120-Day Rate Guarantee:** Applies to insured rates only and 25 Year maximum for amortization.\r\nWhen the application becomes live:\r\n- If current best rates have increased beyond the Rate Hold given, the original Rate Hold expiry applies to the live application.\r\n- If current rates are equal to or less than the Rate Hold, a new 120-day commitment period may be requested.\r\n**Rate Hold Details:**\r\n- Applications are qualified using the greater of the contract rate plus 2% or the Bank of Canada benchmark rate.\r\n- A preapproval rate premium of 20 bps is added to all preapprovals (5-year fixed high-ratio term only).\r\n- When the application becomes live, the prevailing rate is the lesser of the Rate Hold rate and the current best rate at the time of the live deal.\r\n- Maximum of 1 redemption per Rate Hold.\r\n- Buy-downs may be applied only when the application becomes live.\r\n- All rate holds are based on the insured 5-year standard rate with customer-paid insurance\r\n*Note: Rate Holds will not be issued for Promo Rates.* (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
        "isAccepted": null
