        "id": 29,
        "policy": "Purchase Plus Improvement & Refinance Plus Improvement",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Overview**\r\n* The Purchase Plus Improvements (PPI) program allows borrowers to finance the purchase of a home plus the cost of improvements in a single mortgage advance. It\u2019s designed for buyers who need to make upgrades or renovations immediately after purchase.\r\n**Eligibility:**\r\n* Available under Uninsurable, Insured / Insurable CMHC, and Insured / Insurable \u2013 Sagen & Canada Guaranty categories.\r\n**Documentation Required:**\r\n* Detailed list of improvements with contracts and cost estimates.\r\n* Building permit (if structural changes are involved).\r\n**Appraisal Requirements:**\r\n* Must be ordered from MERIX\u2019s approved list.\r\n* Broker provides \u201cas is\u201d and \u201cas complete\u201d valuations.\r\n* Borrower pays appraisal costs (except where insurer requires one, then insurer covers it).\r\n **Maximum Improvement Amounts&**\r\n* Uninsurable: Lesser of $40,000 OR 20% of the property\u2019s initial value.\r\n* CMHC Insured/Insurable: Maximum 10% of \u201cas improved\u201d value.\r\n* Sagen & Canada Guaranty Insured/Insurable: Can exceed $40,000 or 20% of initial value if supported by insurer.\r\n**Solicitor Instructions**\r\n* MERIX advances the entire mortgage to the solicitor at closing.\r\n* Solicitor must hold back the improvement funds until MERIX authorizes release.\r\n* Completion timelines:\r\n* Uninsurable: Within 180 days of advance.\r\n* Insured/Insurable: Within 270 days of advance.\r\n**Requirements for Fund Release**\r\n* Improvements must match approval quotes.\r\n* Confirmation methods:\r\n* > $15,000 or borrower-completed work \u2192 inspection by MERIX-approved appraiser.\r\n* \u2264 $15,000 \u2192 before & after photos plus paid invoices (full appraisal may be required if unclear).\r\n* Broker orders inspection (if needed) or submits documents to MERIX.\r\n* No progress draws allowed.\r\n* Inspection costs are borrower\u2019s responsibility. (Applies: National)",
