        "id": 42,
        "policy": "Bridge Financing",
        "description": "* A bridge loan is a temporary loan that facilitates closings when the purchase of a customer's new home closes before the sale of their current home. Bridge financing allows customers to borrow funds based on the net equity in their current home in situations where that equity is tied up until the closing date of their current home.\r\n* 120 day term\r\n* Rate: P+2%\r\n* Bridge loan fee: $250\r\n* Minimum bridge loan: $5,000\r\n* The maximum bridge loan amount is the lesser of the downpayment required or the net equity in the property being sold\r\n* Calculation of net proceeds is the sale price less existing mortgage(s) balances less 7% of sale price for closing costs\r\n* Collateral mortgage to be registered where the below is applicable:\r\n* Bridge loan is > $150,000 AND/OR\r\n* Bridge loan term exceeds 90 days\r\n* Discharge fee applicable upon bridge loan payout\r\n* Bridge loan payment to be included in TDS when:\r\n* Bridge loan term exceeds 90 days\r\n* Payment calculation based on outstanding balance, 5 year benchmark rate and a 25 year amortization\r\n* Bridge loans are not permitted to facilitate on time closings as a result of land registry system delays in Alberta, Saskatchewan and Manitoba.\r\n* The completion date of the purchase must be prior to the completion date of the sale.\r\n* Requirements\r\n* Copies of the Agreement of Purchase/Sale for both the existing property and the subject property being purchased must be obtained and the following confirmed:\r\n* That both Agreements of Purchase/Sale are binding contracts\r\n* That all conditions have been removed\r\n* Receipt of existing mortgage statement to confirm available equity\r\n* The following documents must be received before the new mortgage is advanced:\r\n* The Solicitor's Acknowledgement\r\n* The Declaration and Direction\r\n* The Promissory Note\r\n* The Assignment of Funds\r\n* The Statement of Adjustments and Direction to Pay/Trust Ledger confirming net sale proceeds equal to or greater than the bridge loan\r\n* Where the sale property is a private/double ended/non-arms length transaction, additional documentation may be required. Underwriter to advise upon review of file submission. (Applies: National)",
        "isAccepted": null
