        "id": 47,
        "policy": "Credit History: Bruised credit, consumer proposals, bankruptcy",
        "description": "- Maximum age of bureau not to exceed:\r\n - 30 days \u2013 firm deal\r\n - 90 days \u2013 preapproval\r\n- Acceptable Credit\r\n - Must have a minimum of 2 active trades with 24 months reporting\r\n - Minimum $1,000 revolving limits or minimum $2,500 original loan amounts\r\n**Consumer Proposal | Bankruptcy**\r\n- May consider borrowers with previous credit counselling, a consumer proposal, OPD or bankruptcy subject to the below, while also taking into consideration overall file strength:\r\n- Insured/Insurable loans only\r\n - Excluding BFS Insured/Insurable, Secondary Homes & Small Rental Program\r\n- Discharged minimum 2 years confirmed via discharge document or current credit bureau confirming date of discharge\r\n- Re-established credit for 2 years after the date of discharge \r\n - 2 active trades with 24 mos reporting\r\n - Minimum $1,000 revolving limits or minimum $2,500 original loan amounts\r\n- Borrowers with more than one consumer proposal or bankruptcy not considered\r\n**Derogatory Credit**\r\n- If any one borrower has 4 or more derogatory credit trades with R4/I4/O4 ratings or higher, (including historical ratings) must provide:\r\n - Reasons for credit delinquency (past & present)\r\n - All debts that are currently reporting worse than \u201c1\u201d are required to be brought current prior to funding\r\n - All revolving debts that are currently in excess of their limit are to be paid down prior to funding\r\n - Collections, judgments or delinquencies that are still reporting as outstanding are to be paid in full and confirmation must be provided prior to funding\r\n**Previous Bankrupt Clients:**\r\n* Insured/Insurable. \r\n* Owner Occupied.\r\n* Excludes BFS clients. \r\n* Discharged minimum 2 years confirmed via discharge document or current credit bureau confirming date of discharge.\r\n* Re-established credit for 2 years after the date of discharge.\r\n* Minimum 2 re-established trades with a $1000.00 limit from a recognized financial institution. \r\n* No real estate included in bankruptcy. (Applies: National)",
