        "id": 48,
        "policy": "Debt Servicing",
        "description": "* Revolving Trades: 3% of outstanding balance.\r\n* Instalment Loans: Payment on credit bureau.\r\n* Line of Credit: Payment on credit bureau if reporting or 3% of balance, if not in repayment.* Student Line of Credit: If LOC is not yet amortized and not yet in repayment: 1.50% of outstanding balance to be used.\r\n* If LOC is amortized and in repayment: actual payment to be used.\r\n* Debt service 3% closing costs.\r\n* HELOC - use BOC rate at balance over 25 years .\r\n**Exceptions related to Debt Servicing**\r\n* For example a company car paid for by work and to remove from debt servicing.\r\n* We would normally want 12-24 months of payment history, reporting on the financials as an expense.\r\n* Better chances if it were insured/insurable file too.\r\n* Need to reviewed on a case by case basis\r\n**LOC Secured:** \r\n* Payment to be calculated on the outstanding balance using the contract rate and 25 year amortization \r\n* If contract rate is unknown, benchmark rate is to be used (Applies: National)",
