        "id": 83,
        "policy": "Submission Tips & Underwriting Assistance",
        "description": "**Credit Bureaus**\r\n* Merix uses Equifax\r\n* Yes, TransUnion accepted \r\n**Please note the only files that must be resubmitted are for the following reasons**\r\n* Client changes ownership\r\n* Adding a borrower \r\n* Forgetting to add a property\r\n**Please just send a message via the portal if a customer ever decides to:**\r\n* Change from fixed to variable rate\r\n* File was submitted as purchase and becomes purchase + Reno\r\n* Client changes the down payment\r\n* Closing date changes\r\n**Here are some helpful tips**\r\n* QUICK CLOSINGS: Upload documents when you submit, mention if you can or cannot extend closing in your loan notes. Call your BDM to discuss.\r\n* PURCHASE PLUS IMPROVEMENT: Upon submission upload Purchase Agreement, MLS and quote for improvements. We do this program very well! \r\n* INCOME: If you have ANY concerns with the income, please provide as much income documentation upfront as you can. \r\n If you use OTHER for income, please indicate in your loan notes the income details. \r\n* DOWN PAYMENT: Please be accurate in sources of down payment. If from savings, ask upfront: will the lender see any large deposits? Note the source of those large deposits. \r\n If you use OTHER for source of down payment, please indicate source in your loan notes. \r\n* MARITAL STATUS: Review the credit report for the AKA (previous last name). If separated, provide separation agreement upfront.\r\n* CONDITION OF FINANCING : Email your Underwriter and enter the COF date in the notes, so we can prioritize the application. Reach out to me on this one too if needed.\r\n* NON-SUBJECT RENTAL INCOME: Please provide T1 Generals upfront for any rentals owned for more than a year. Along with our rental worksheet.\r\n**SUBMISSION TIPS (General)**:\r\n* Submitting deals \u2013 choose MERIX Trailer residual income) or Merix Standard (maximize upfront\r\ncompensation).\r\n* Credit bureaus not older than 30 days when submitting. SIN#.\r\n* Mitigate derogatory late payments. Shelter Costs? Heat?\r\n* Private/Estate or Power of sale, COF? Bridge.\r\n* MLS listing; is there anything the underwriter should know? Zoning \u2013 RESIDENTIAL.\r\n* Income: advise if there are multiple sources, probation, does the LOE match the paystub? Work\r\nfor family?\r\n* Down payment; be specific if down payment from multiple sources.\r\n* Agents submitting under your account? Agents to add their contact details in the notes.\r\n* Advise the rate you need in your deal notes. Advise if you require a bridge. Purpose of ETO.\r\n* No previous bankrupts or consumer proposals.\r\n* Add assets\r\n**SUBMISSION TIPS (Switches and Transfers)**: \r\n* Advise if the switch is a Collateral/Non-Collateral in the deal notes\r\n* Let us know the original loan amount/funding date and remaining amortization\r\n* Insurer name & number\r\n* Include your contact details in the submission notes\r\n* Indicate the rate in the submission notes (ex. HR 5 year fixed and rate)\r\n**SignUp**\r\n- Need agents to submit under an active account holder. We allow individual agents along with broker-owners to open an account, there is an agreement involved to have access. \r\n- All submissions need to be submitted through an active MERIX Financial broker. (Applies: National)",
        "isAccepted": null
