        "description": "[ACCEPTED] Acceptable forms of Pension.\r\n* Federal and or Provincial programs (CPP or OAS)\r\n* Canadian Company or Government Employee pension\r\n* Foreign Pensions that are paid into a Canadian bank account, and income is declared and taxed in Canada.\r\nNon-Taxable Pension:\r\n* Eligible gross up is allowed upon underwriter approval\r\n* Must be defined non-taxable by the Income Tax Act of Canada (CCRA)\r\n* Less than $30,000 maximum 25% gross up\r\n* Equal to or greater than $30,000 maximum 35% Gross up\r\nPension Documentation Requirements:\r\n* CPP, OAS: Most recent T4A slip supported by most recent bank statement/pension stub to show the direct deposit\r\n* Canadian or Foreign company or Government employee: current pay stub or bank statement to show direct deposit dated within 30 days as well as one of the following: Most recent 2 years T4A\u2019s, Most recent 2 years NOAs, a letter from the previous employer/pension administrator confirming pension amount\r\n* Current investment statement dated within 60 days fo application date AND \r\n* Most recent 2-year history of income via one of the following: NOAs + full T1s, T5s, T4As, OR T4RIFs. (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
