        "policy": "Income - Salaried, Hourly, Contract, Part-Time, Bonus or Casual",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] * Employment history of the most recent 2 years must be provided.\r\n**Letter of Employment (LOE)**\r\n* To be on company letterhead with address and phone number and include all of the elements listed below.\r\n* Author\u2019s name, title & signature (someone of authority - i.e. Immediate Manager, HR department, Owner)\r\n* Dated within 60 days of application date\r\n* Full First and Last name of employee\r\n* Annual Base Salary or Hourly rate\r\n* Length of Employment (Start Date)\r\n* Position\r\n* Status (full time, part time, contract, etc.)\r\n* Prospect for continued employment\r\n**Paystubs**\r\n* Issued in the last 30 days\r\n **Pending Increases**\r\n* Must be confirmed by the employer in writing prior to funding\r\n **T1 Generals**\r\n* Cannot be used in isolation, must be supported by the corresponding NOA\r\n **Income Streams**\r\n* The number of income sources must be reasonable and sustainable.\r\n **Additional Income Types**\r\n* Other income in addition to base hourly/salary/commission rate, such as overtime or part-time income may be used for qualification purposes provided the income has been received consistently for 2 years. Please see the applicable section for further breakdown of documents required (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
