        "id": 40,
        "policy": "Appraisals",
        "description": "* RMG will require an appraisal on; all partner/spousal buy-outs, conventional deals, private sales, rural properties, double-ended transactions and power of sale/foreclosure\r\n* RMG Appraisal rebate program works for purchase plus inspections as well\r\n* Must be ordered through an approved RMG Appraiser or through NAS and Solidify. To access list of appraisers go to [Click on Link](https://gateway.rmgmortgages.ca) under Tools/Quick Links.\r\nRMG will require Full Appraisals where the file;\r\n1. Falls within 65% - 80% LTV (under 65% we can most often request a Drive-By Appraisal) \r\n2. Regardless of LTV, even with CMHC/Sagen insurance obtained, where the file is a; \r\n* Private Sale \r\n* Spousal/Partner Buy-Out \r\n* Double-Ended Transactions \r\n* Rural properties \r\n* Foreclosure \r\nRemember to keep a copy of the paid invoice to send to your BDM once the deal has funded to be processed for our Appraisal Rebate. \r\n* If RMG requests an appraisal, and the deal funds- it is eligible for our appraisal rebate based on following tiered guideline; \r\nMortgage Amount $250K = $300 rebate\r\n* All rebates are issued via EFT (Electronic Funds Transfer) to the bank account on file for your office broker commission payments. If you are offering to repay your client or appraiser, you will need to take care of this from your end as RMG no longer sends manual appraisal rebate cheque's, nor directs the payment to anyone other than the registered submission agent for your team. Your payroll department will receive email notification of the payment and file name/number the rebate applies too\r\n**Drive-by Appraisal**\r\nIs an assessment of the property that does not require an inspection of the subject property's interior.\r\n* Eligible for RMG Appraisal Rebate Program\r\n* Owner Occupied\r\n* Purchase: LTV ratio is <65% in Urban centers with a minimum population of 100,000\r\n* Transaction is arm\u2019s length\r\n* Property is listed on MLS\r\n* Transaction is not double-ended (purchase and seller are represented by different agents)\r\n* Refinance: LTV ratio is <65% in Urban centres with a minimum population of 100,000\r\n* Transfers:LTV ratio is </= 65% in Urban centres with a minimum population of 50,000 AND\r\nExisting insurance details have not been validated\r\nNote: The lower of mid-range value or the purchase price is to be used for calculating the loan to value.\r\n**Full Appraisal**\r\nIs a full assessment of the property including the property's interior. The appraisal will contain, but not limited to documented comparable sales, rental income if applicable, the current state of repair, including pictures of any deficiencies identified for both the interior and exterior etc.\r\n*Eligible for RMG Appraisal Rebate Program\r\n*Required, but not limited to:\r\n*Equity Buyout: uninsurable and insurable loans \r\n*LTV is from 65% up to 80% and AVM is ineligible\r\n*LTV <65% and AVM ineligible\r\n**Realty Tax Assessment**\r\n\u200b* Standard and Collateral Transfer programs only:\r\n* Loan to value (LTV) ratio is </=65% of the assessed value (based on the Realty Tax Assessment) in lending areas where the population is greater than 200,000 AND\r\n* Existing insurance details have not been validated\r\n* Condos are ineligible. (Applies: Alberta, British Columbia, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland & Labrador, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan)",
