        "policy": "Non Permanent Residents",
        "description": "[NOT ACCEPTED] * Starting January 1, 2023, non-Canadians will no longer be able to purchase property for a period of 2 years.\r\n* EXCEPT for foreign nationals who:\r\n* Are temporary residents with a valid Canadian work permit. Workers and holders of a temporary resident permit may also have temporary resident status. Only foreign nationals physically in Canada have temporary resident status.\r\n* Have asylum in Canada.\r\n* Are purchasing real estate with their spouse or common-law partner who is a Canadian citizen, Indigenous person, or a permanent or temporary resident with a valid work permit.\r\n* A common-law partner is understood to mean someone who has lived with you for at least 1 year.\r\n* International students in the process of obtaining permanent residence\r\n* It\u2019s the broker\u2019s responsibility to check whether the borrower falls under one of the above-mentioned exceptions before submitting a foreign investor application to the centre. If the application does not meet the requirements, it will be automatically declined (Applies: Ontario, Quebec)",
