        "id": 19,
        "policy": "Mobiles & Modulars",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **What**\r\n- Financing available for the purchase/refinance of a mobile home (detached residential dwelling designed for transport) as determined by the method in which it is affixed to the ground.\r\n**Who**\r\n- For someone who would like to buy, construct, or refinance a mobile home that is permanently affixed to owned land.\r\n**Benefits**\r\n- Provides a conventional or high-ratio mortgage solution for non-tradition dwelling with flexibility of multiple mortgage options. There are 2 types of loan solutions available to meet member's needs: Collateral Mortgage and Residential Mortgage.\r\n***Product Features***\r\n- Available for Principal Residences or Vacation properties. Due to the 35 year Standard Economic Life, HELOCs on these properties are ineligible. Rentals are also ineligible.\r\n- Mobile Homes on Leased Land (ie. Chattel Loans) are not available for financing through the Broker Channel.\r\n***Collateral Mortgage****\r\n- Purpose\r\n - Purchase, New Construction, or Refinance\r\n- Eligible Property Types\r\n - Borrower owns the land, home is not permanently affixed (or cannot be verified as such)\r\n- Maximum LTV\r\n - Conventional financing at 65% LTV only\r\n- Security\r\n - Secured by residential mortgage against the land, and a General Security Agreement (GSA) against the home\r\n- Rentals\r\n - Not eligible for consideration\r\n_NOTE:_ Collateral Mortgage not eligible through the Mortgage Development Channel unless home is permanently affixed.\r\n***Residential Mortgage****\r\n- Purpose\r\n - Purchase, New Construction, or Refinance\r\n- Eligible Property Types\r\n - Borrower owns the land, home is permanently affixed by foundation/grade beam/weld to pilings in accordance to CSA standards\r\n- Maximum LTV\r\n - Available as Conventional (75% LTV) or High-Ratio (LTV subject to insurer's current program in place)\r\n- Security\r\n - Secured by a residential mortgage against the property (*see applicable Residential Mortgage product type)\r\n- Rentals\r\n - Eligible for consideration\r\n**Interest Rate**\r\n- Rates: See Broker Rate Sheet for current rates/terms per applicable mortgage terms\r\n- Terms Available: Fixed or Variable\r\n- Max Amortization: 25 years, subject to Remaining Economic Life (see Amortization)\r\n**Appraisals**\r\n- We would like to inform you of an update to our appraisal requirements, specifically concerning mobile homes processed through our channel.\r\n- Up-front appraisal (dated within 3 months) is required on conventional Mobile Home requests. Ordered by broker. Member is responsible for all fees.\r\n- High Ratio insurers (CMHC or Sagen) will order their own appraisal if the stated value cannot be substantiated as submitted.\r\n- Only mobile homes with a Canadian Standard Association (CSA) certification label are eligible for financing. The Serial Number and CSA Number of the home must be verified by the appraiser and recorded on the appraisal.\r\n**Amortization**\r\n- Maximum amortization is 25 years, however it is also subject to the Remaining Economic Life (REL) of the home as indicated within the appraisal.\r\n - Conventional: The lesser of 25 years or Remaining Economic Life, as determined by an appraisal\r\n - High Ratio: As per insurer guidelines. SCU guidelines: If there is no appraisal, 35 years less age of home. If there is an appraisal, the lesser of 25 years or the Remaining Economic Life.\r\n**Fire Insurance**\r\n- An assignment covering Fire Insurance with loss payable to Servus Credit Union must be provided for the file, with the value of the insurance sufficient to cover the loan advance.\r\n**Blend and Extend**\r\n- Blend and extend rates are valid for 30 days and subject to change based on the closing date, outstanding balance on the current mortgage, and funding date of the new mortgage. The term selected must be the same or greater than the previous term. Applies to fixed rates only.\r\n**Requirements**\r\n- **Permanent Affixation:** The mobile home must be permanently affixed to owned land. Leased land will not be considered eligible for financing.\r\n- **Remaining Economic Life:** The appraiser will be tasked with confirming the remaining economic life of the mobile home.\r\n- **Loan-to-Value (LTV) Ratios:**\r\n - Conventional Loans: We can allow up to 75% LTV.\r\n - High Ratio Loans: We can allow from 80% to 95% LTV.\r\n- **Identification Documentation:** We require a CSA or serial number for the mobile home. Please note that there are no exceptions to this requirement.\r\n- It is imperative that these requirements are met for any mobile home financing applications submitted through our channel. Adhering to these guidelines will streamline the process and ensure smoother transactions for all parties involved (Applies: Alberta)",
