        "id": 20,
        "policy": "New to Canada",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **New to Canada Residential Mortgage Program Requirements**\r\n**Eligible Borrowers**\r\n* New to Canada applicants may include:\r\n* Permanent Residents who have immigrated to Canada within the last 5 years\r\n* Temporary residents who are:\r\n* Working in Canada, or\r\n* Studying in Canada\r\n* Applicants must be living and working/studying in Canada at the time of application.\r\n* Permanent Resident Documentation\r\n* One of the following is required:\r\n* Permanent Resident Card showing \u201cPR Since\u201d date, or\r\n* Confirmation of Permanent Residence showing \u201cBecame PR on\u201d date\r\n**Borrower Eligibility**\r\n* Eligible for First-Time Home Buyers purchasing an owner-occupied property in Canada\r\n* Non-first-time buyers must qualify under standard mortgage guidelines\r\n**Property Requirements**\r\n* Eligible properties must be:\r\n* MLS-listed resale properties, or\r\n* New construction by a reputable residential home builder\r\n* Not eligible:\r\n* Private sales\r\n* Self-builds\r\n**Maximum Limits**\r\n* Maximum purchase price (Conventional): $1,000,000\r\n* Maximum amortization:\r\n* High Ratio: Up to 30 years, per insurer guidelines\r\n* Conventional: Up to 25 years\r\n**Conventional Mortgages. 20% to 34.99% down**\r\n* Applicants must have a proven source of income\r\n* If employed with the same employer for less than six months:\r\n* 12 months of mortgage payments must be held on deposit with Servus\r\n* Funds:\r\n* Held in a separate demand account\r\n* May be used to service mortgage payments if required\r\n* Exception:\r\n* Permanent Resident Healthcare Professionals\r\n* Employed in Canada for six months or more\r\n* Valid professional license and employment start date confirmation required\r\n* Deposit requirement waived\r\n* May qualify under the Professional Lending Program\r\n**35% down**\r\n* Applicant must be employed and working in Canada\r\n* Proof of employment must be retained on file\r\n* Stated income may be used when:\r\n* Reasonable for the industry and role\r\n* Authorized as non-conforming\r\n* 12 months of mortgage payments may be required on deposit with Servus\r\n* Deposit requirement is waived if down payment is 40% or greater at origination\r\n**Non-Eligible Under This Program**\r\n* (Unless qualified under standard conventional guidelines)\r\n* Refinances\r\n* Equity take-outs\r\n* Private sales\r\n* Self-builds\r\n* Purchases restricted under the Prohibition on the Purchase of Residential Property by Non-Canadians Act\r\n* Home Equity Lines of Credit (HELOCs) (Applies: Alberta)",
