        "id": 29,
        "policy": "Rentals - Income",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] * All rental income used for qualification must be derived from residential properties that are rentable at the time of application.\r\n* Speculative rental income is not permitted. Examples include:\r\n* Basement suites that are not yet completed\r\n* Properties undergoing major renovations and not currently rentable\r\n* Future rental income that cannot be verified\r\n* Additionally, titles for all properties being used for rental income must be included with the application. This allows us to confirm there are no builder's liens, pending litigation, or other title concerns.\r\n**Types of Rental Income**\r\n* Rental properties fall into two categories:\r\n* Owner-Occupied Properties\r\n* (Legal Secondary Suite or Garage Suite)\r\n* Non-Owner-Occupied Rental Properties\r\n* (Standalone rental properties)\r\n* Owner-Occupied Legal Suites\r\n* Only income from legal and conforming secondary suites can be used.\r\n* Income from illegal or non-conforming suites cannot be considered.\r\n**Acceptable Documentation**\r\n* Preferred:\r\n* T776 Statement of Real Estate Rentals\r\n* Complete T1 General\r\n* Corresponding Notice of Assessment\r\n* If the suite was recently rented or purchased and a T776 is not available:\r\n* Active lease agreement\r\n* Minimum 3 months of rental deposits into a Canadian financial institution account\r\n* Deposit amounts must match the lease agreement\r\n* If there is no active lease:\r\n* Current appraisal confirming market rent\r\n* If an appraisal provides a rental range, use the midpoint of the range.\r\n**Income Treatment**\r\n* Subject Property\r\n* Use 50% of gross monthly rent\r\n* Enter all associated property expenses\r\n* Existing Property\r\n* T776 or lease agreement: Use 100% of gross monthly rent\r\n* Appraisal: Use 50% of market rent\r\n* Enter all associated property expenses\r\n* Non-Owner-Occupied Rental Properties\r\n**Acceptable Documentation**\r\n* Preferred:\r\n* T776 Statement of Real Estate Rentals\r\n* Complete T1 General\r\n* Corresponding Notice of Assessment\r\n* If not available:\r\n* Active lease agreement\r\n* Minimum 3 months of rental deposits\r\n* Deposits must match lease agreement\r\n* If no lease is available:\r\n* Current appraisal confirming market rent\r\n* If an appraisal provides a rental range, use the midpoint of the range.\r\n**Rental Income Calculator**\r\n* For all non-owner-occupied rental properties, the Rental Income Calculator must be used.\r\n* The calculator:\r\n* Determines net rental income or deficit\r\n* Accounts for ownership percentages\r\n* Calculates allowable expenses\r\n* Produces the rental income figure used for qualification\r\n* Please see rental income calculator attached.\r\n**Common Submission Reminders**\r\n* When submitting a file that includes rental income, please ensure you provide:\r\n* Current title(s) for all rental properties\r\n* T776, T1 General, and NOA (where available)\r\n* Lease agreements\r\n* Proof of rental deposits\r\n* Market rent appraisal (if required)\r\n* Mortgage statements for existing rental properties\r\n* Ownership details for all rental properties\r\n* Providing these documents upfront helps avoid delays and allows our team to review the file more efficiently.\r\n* Please note that while all applications must follow Servus policy guidelines, brokers can also review the individual insurer programs for high-ratio rental property applications through CMHC, Sagen, and Canada Guaranty.\r\n* As a friendly reminder, please send all inquiries and supporting documentation to BrokerMortgages@servus.ca, as emails and voicemails sent to personal email addresses or direct lines are not monitored.\r\n* As always, we're happy to see your inquiries come in and look forward to supporting your rental property financing scenarios. Have a great week ahead! (Applies: Alberta)",
