        "policy": "Condos",
        "description": "**Condominium Guidelines**\r\n**Eligible Condo Types**\r\n* Apartment-style condominiums\r\n* Duplexes, townhouses, or row-style units (when legally structured as condominiums)\r\n* Owner-occupied or rental units\r\n**Key Eligibility Criteria**\r\n* Units must be self-contained, meaning:\r\n* Must have a private entrance, kitchen, bathroom, and crucially \u2014 in-suite laundry\r\n**Special Property Considerations (Case-by-Case Review)**\r\n* Condo Conversions: Allowed if units are self-contained and have in-suite laundry\r\n* Post-Tension Cables: Require a structural engineer's report verifying the integrity of the building\r\n* Age-Restricted Buildings: Acceptable on conventional deals only\r\n* Shared utilities (e.g., shared well, shared septic): Not eligible. (Applies: Alberta)",
