        "policy": "Down Payment",
        "description": "Personal Savings\r\nMinimum 3 months (90 days) of account statements for all accounts contributing to the down payment.\r\nStatements must confirm:\r\nAccount ownership\r\nCurrent balance\r\nFull transaction history\r\nThe source of any large deposits must be explained and documented.\r\nSale Proceeds\r\nNet funds from the sale of an existing property.\r\nFully signed firm (unconditional) Sale Agreement\r\nAll addendums and waivers confirming conditions have been removed\r\nCurrent mortgage balance statement\r\nSale proceeds must support the amount of down payment being used for the new purchase.\r\nRRSP / FHSA Withdrawals\r\nWithdrawals from a Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) or First Home Savings Account (FHSA).\r\nEvidence confirming eligibility to withdraw funds\r\nMost recent 3 months of statements\r\nDocumentation supporting the withdrawal, where available\r\nExisting Equity in Owned Property\r\nBorrowing against equity in an existing property.\r\nCurrent mortgage balance statement\r\nMost recent property tax assessment\r\nAn appraisal may be required at the lender's discretion. (No changes noted from your original wording.)\r\nThe notable update is that FHSA withdrawals are now explicitly included alongside RRSP withdrawals, and the personal savings requirements now specifically call out current balance and full transaction history on the statements (Applies: Alberta)",
