        "policy": "Income - Other Taxable",
        "description": "Variable Employment Income\r\nApplies to:\r\nBonus\r\nCasual\r\nContract\r\nLiving Allowance\r\nOvertime\r\nSecondary Employment\r\nShift Differential\r\nTips\r\nTrades & Labour\r\nVehicle Allowance\r\nVariable employment income is verified using both a Primary Method and a Secondary Method.\r\nTotal earnings calculated using the Primary Method must be equal to or greater than the Secondary Method.\r\nIf the Primary Method results in a lower amount, the lower income will be used for qualification.\r\nPrimary Method\r\nProvide one of the following:\r\nCurrent pay stub showing year-to-date (YTD) earnings.\r\nTotal YTD earnings (including all fixed and variable income) must equal or exceed the Secondary Method.\r\nSecondary Method\r\nProvide two of the following:\r\nMost recent Notice of Assessment (NOA) or Proof of Income Statement\r\nMost recent T4/T4A\r\nPrevious year-end pay stub\r\nIncome Calculation\r\nQualifying income is based on the lesser of the current year's income or the two-year average.\r\nIneligible Fluctuating Income\r\nIncome from gig economy or similar fluctuating sources is not accepted, including:\r\nAirbnb\r\nUber\r\nLyft\r\nDoorDash (Applies: Alberta)",
