        "description": "Property Types\r\nPrincipal Residence & Second Home (Up to $1,000,000 | \u226440 Acres)\r\nMaximum 80% LTV\r\nMaximum 30-year amortization\r\nValuation includes the residence, outbuildings, and full land size\r\nRural properties with no active farming or business on-site are eligible\r\nPrincipal Residence (Up to $1,000,000 | 40.01\u2013160 Acres)\r\nMaximum 75% LTV\r\nMaximum 25-year amortization\r\nLTV exceptions are not available\r\nLTVs above 75% require high-ratio financing\r\nValuation includes the residence and full land size (outbuildings excluded)\r\nRural properties with no active farming or business on-site are eligible\r\nRental Property (\u226440 Acres)\r\nMaximum 80% LTV\r\nMaximum 25-year amortization\r\nMarket rents may be used\r\nRental Property (40.01\u2013160 Acres)\r\nMaximum 75% LTV\r\nMaximum 25-year amortization\r\nMarket rents may be used\r\nProperties Over $1,000,000\r\nSubject to a sliding-scale LTV:\r\n80% of the first $1,000,000\r\n50% of the remaining value\r\nExceptions may be considered\r\nManufactured Homes\r\nMust be permanently affixed to owned land\r\nAppraisal must include the year, make, model, serial number, and CSA number\r\nOutbuildings may be included in the valuation\r\nPurchase Plus Improvements\r\nAppraisal must include both \"as is\" and \"as complete\" values\r\nLending value is based on the lesser of:\r\nThe appraised \"as improved\" value, or\r\nThe purchase price plus the cost of improvements\r\nRefinances Plus Improvements\r\nConventional financing only\r\nLending value is based on the lesser of:\r\nThe appraised \"as improved\" value, or\r\nThe appraised \"as is\" value plus the cost of improvements\r\nRaw Land (\u226440 Acres)\r\nMaximum 75% LTV\r\nMaximum 20-year amortization\r\nRaw Land (40.01\u2013160 Acres)\r\nMaximum 65% LTV\r\nMaximum 20-year amortization\r\nIneligible Properties & Products\r\nSelf-build construction\r\nAirbnb and short-term rental properties\r\nRental pool properties\r\nCommercial properties\r\nCo-operatives\r\nConstruction draw mortgages outside Alberta or Saskatchewan\r\nFormer or current grow-ops\r\nProperties located more than 150 km from a Servus branch in Alberta (50 km in Saskatchewan)\r\nProperties located outside Alberta or Saskatchewan\r\nMobile or modular homes not permanently affixed to owned land\r\nShop/House (Shouse)\r\nTiny homes\r\nOut-of-province rental properties\r\nFractional ownership\r\nTimeshares\r\nVacation rental properties\r\nWood boiler as the primary heat source\r\nShared well or open discharge septic systems\r\nPark models (fall under Servus' RV Policy)\r\nWood Foundation Properties\r\nEligible subject to additional requirements\r\nFCT must receive engineered or architectural approved plans\r\nWood foundation must be pressure-treated with preservative chemicals to prevent decay\r\nBuilder must provide confirmation that materials meet CSA standards (Applies: Alberta)",
