        "description": "* Residences that are currently owner-occupied or to be purchased and occupied by the applicant and held in single or joint tenancy .\r\n* Single family dwellings.\r\n* Multiple family dwellings (maximum four units), with one of the units owner-occupied unless being financed under the Investment Property Program.\r\n* Registered condominium units.\r\n* Maximum lot size of 25 acres with maximum property value based on house + 5 acres only and no outbuildings (confirmed via full appraisal).\r\n* Modular or Manufactured homes provided it is permanently affixed and complies with the Mortgage Insurer\u2019s enhanced guidelines.\r\n* Second Homes property requirements:\r\n o Foundation must be permanent and installed beyond the frost line.\r\n o Must be zoned and used as residential, rural, or seasonal. No mixed uses or rental pooling.\r\n o Freehold or condominium title. No co-ops or \u00bc interest ownership.\r\n o At minimum, property must have a kitchen, 3-piece bathroom, bedroom, and common area.\r\n o Year-round road access on reasonable quality public roads, serviced by the local municipality.\r\n o Property must be winterized with a permanent heat source.\r\n o Good quality construction with no signs of deferred maintenance.\r\n o Water source: well, municipal serviced, and cistern.\r\n o There must be good market appeal in the area with no adverse influences/neighborhood nuisances.\" (Applies: National)",
        "isAccepted": null
