        "description": "Rental Offset Policy:\r\nNumber of Rental Properties* (Including Basement, Upper suite or Carriage home of primary residence) & Maximum Rental Offset**\r\n* Owner-occupied with basement/upper suite and/or carriage home*** (max. 2 rental suites) - 80% \r\n* 1-2 Non-owner occupied rental units - 75%\r\n* 3-4 Non-owner occupied rental units - 70%\r\n* More than 4 non-owner occupied rental units including those financed at other FI's are considered a business operation and therefore must be referred to the Commercial division\r\nNotes: Thie above includes properties financed by Coastal and/or other FI's and C/T (clear title) properties\r\n*Number of rental properties: refers to the total number of units owned by the member(s) including the subject property being financed.\r\n**How calculation works: an individual with more than 2 non-owner occupied rental units will result in a maximum rental offset of 70% on all the non-owner occupied rental units. However, an owner-occupied basement suite may continue to be calculated with an 80% rental offset.\r\n***Primary residence with suite: Income is allowable from a maximum of two suites on the owner-occupied property (eg. basement, upper suite and/or carriage home). Room & board cannot be considered as income, as this is typically being received from a temporary student that is renting a room and not a suite (Applies: British Columbia)",
