        "description": "- Purchases of Primary Owner-Occupied Properties\r\n- FICO score 680 and above for at least one borrower: TDSR 44% GDSR 39%\r\n- FICO score less than 680 for all borrowers: TDSR 42% GDSR 35%\r\n- Note: GDSR does not apply to rental properties or secondary homes.\r\n- Refinance, Rental and Secondary Homes - Conventional Financing, Regardless of FICO score: TDSR 42%\r\n- Refinance of Primary Owner Occupied Property Conventional, Regardless of FICO score:GDSR 35%.\r\nDebt Servicing\r\nCredit cards & lines of credit: Use the greater of 3% of the outstanding balance or the payment reported on the credit bureau.\r\nIf no payment is reported on the bureau, use 3% of the outstanding balance.\r\nStudent loans (Alberta/Canada) with no reported payment: Calculate at Prime + 2.5%, amortized over a maximum of 10 years.\r\nSecured lines of credit: Amortize the outstanding balance over 25 years using the contract rate or Bank of Canada 5-year benchmark rate (Applies: Alberta)",
