        "id": 74,
        "policy": "Pre-Payment Penalties",
        "description": "* Best rate to best rate. The Prepayment clause in a Full Penalty mortgage may provide for a penalty, which is the greater of:\r\n* Three (3) months interest on the amount prepaid, if any;\r\n* The amount, if any, by which interest at the Mortgage Rate exceeds interest at the \"\"Prevailing Rate\"\" calculated on the amount prepaid for a term commencing on the Prepayment Date and ending on the Balance Due Date;\r\n* If a mortgage is not due for more than five years after the date of the mortgage, the borrower may pay the balance of the mortgage in full any time after the five-year period upon payment of three (3) months' interest (e.g. 10 year term) (Applies: British Columbia)",
