        "description": "Gifted Down Payment / Gifted Equity\r\nGifted funds are acceptable from an immediate family member, generally a spouse, parent, child, grandparent, brother or sister.\r\nRequire a signed and dated gift letter confirming:\r\nAmount of the gift.\r\nGift is being provided toward the purchase of the home.\r\nGift does not need to be repaid.\r\nDonor\u2019s relationship to the borrower.\r\nGifted funds must be confirmed in the borrower\u2019s possession 15 days prior to closing.\r\nGifted equity from the subject property is also acceptable and is typically provided by an immediate family member.\r\nFor gifted equity, require a lawyer-drawn purchase agreement, with the gifted equity outlined in the offer to purchase.\r\nA title search/purview of the property is required to confirm ownership. (Applies: Ontario)",
