        "id": 73,
        "policy": "Shelter Costs",
        "description": "**Minimum Housing Cost**\r\n- $400 Housing Cost per month of minimum housing cost should be added as an expense unless the primary borrower holds a primary residence title or actual rental expense is already included as an expense as part of GDS/TDS.\r\n- Minimum housing cost should be calculated per person, with exemption to spouses living at same address.\r\n- Minimum housing cost can be waived if the borrower lives with parents, verified through same last name and address. Proof of relationship may be required if the last names of a parent and the borrower are different.\r\n- For a foreign income earner, $400 per month of minimum housing cost should be added as an expense as part of GDS/TDS, unless the person owns a primary residence in the foreign country or rents without ongoing rental expenses (e.g., \"Jeon Se\" in Korea), or actual rental expense is already included as an expense as part of GDS/TDS.\r\n- Minimum housing cost cannot be waived for a foreign income earner (Applies: British Columbia, Ontario)",
