        "policy": "Sliding Scale",
        "description": "The sliding scale on maximum LTV is based on the property value and the geographic location. \r\n**Tier 1**\r\n- ***Detached / Semi-Detached House / Townhouse:*** \r\n - 80% up to 1$ $1,750K\r\n - 70% of the remaining value\r\n- ***Condominium / Condo Townhouse***\r\n - 80% up to 1s $1,250K\r\n - 70% of the remaining value\r\n**Tier 2**\r\n- ***Detached / Semi-Detached House / Townhouse:*** \r\n - 80% up to 1st $1,500K\r\n - 70% of the remaining value\r\n- ***Condominium / Condo Townhouse***\r\n - 80% up to 1st $1,000K\r\n - 70% of the remaining value\r\n**Tier 3**\r\n- ***Detached / Semi-Detached House / Townhouse:*** \r\n - 80% up to 1st $1,250K\r\n - 70% of the remaining value\r\n- ***Condominium / Condo Townhouse***\r\n - 80% up to 1st $750K\r\n - 70% of the remaining value\r\n**Tier 4**\r\n- ***Detached / Semi-Detached House / Townhouse:*** \r\n - 80% up to 1st $1,000K\r\n - 70% of the remaining value\r\n- ***Condominium / Condo Townhouse***\r\n - 80% up to 1st $500K\r\n - 70% of the remaining value\r\n- The Bank may change the sliding scale and Tier classification of regions without notice.\r\n- Since the list does not include all cities and towns in Canada, properties in regions not specified in the list shall be classified into higher subdivisions.\r\n* refer to the appendix document listed in the document section on Spotlight for further details (Applies: British Columbia, Ontario)",
