        "id": 22,
        "policy": "Income - Foster & Adoption Income",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Foster Care Income**\r\n100% of foster parent income will be considered, subject to the following requirements:\r\n- Caregivers must have at least 2 yrs. experience as foster parents. Will be validated with current long-term agreement. If emergency foster care, we would require a 2YR income history. Foster care income cannot account for more than 50% total application income.\r\n- Letter of income or contract from the Ministry responsible for foster care and paystub are required. \r\n- 2 yr. average from the most recent NOA &T1 Generals or T5007 .\r\n- Lender must have a letter from the government social services confirming the tenure of the applicants and the current approved status. \r\n- Maximum number of children in care should not exceed 6 (including any children of their own).\r\n- Applicants must be the owner and occupy the subject property. (Applies: Alberta, Ontario)",
