        "policy": "Purchase Plus Improvement & Refinance Plus Improvement",
        "description": "[ACCEPTED] **Purchase Plus Improvements \u2013 Insurer Program (Sagen)**\r\n**Loan Purpose:** Provide Borrowers with access to funds to make immediate improvements on their purchased homes as soon as they take possession.\r\n**LTV:**\r\n- 95% for 1-2 units (must be owner-occupied).\r\n- 90% for 3-4 units (must be owner-occupied).\r\n**Mortgage Amount:**\r\n- LTV > 80%: Property value must be less than $1,500,000.\r\n- LTV \u2264 80%: Property value must be less than $1,000,000.\r\n**PPI Highlights:**\r\n- PPI can be from $5K \u2013 $80K, exceptions and beyond may be considered.\r\n- Multiple advances to a maximum of two (2), excluding property purchase. Advances managed by lender.\r\n- Borrower may be allowed to complete improvements based on underwriter approval. Must note on PPI form which improvements are being completed by borrower and material quotes must be provided.\r\n**Process:**\r\n- **Initial Approval:** Must provide a completed PPI form on the application. PPI form is available in Nexus Broker Portal.\r\n- **Upfront Release:** An initial release of up to 95% of the property's approved value (less the estimated cost of renovations) will be disbursed first.\r\n- **Holdback:** The remaining funds will be kept in a solicitor's trust account until the completed work is verified by:\r\n1. An inspection report, and/or\r\n2. An official statement from a certified appraiser, and/or\r\n3. A final invoice from the contractor\r\n- **Payment Verification:** You must also provide proof that the contractor has been paid in full before these remaining funds can be released.\r\n- **Final Disbursement Condition:** The final payout will only be authorized once the completed work fully aligns with the initial quote or contract submitted with your application.\r\n**Borrower Qualifications:**\r\n- A minimum credit bureau score of 680 is recommended where loan-to-value ratio is 80% or greater. Where loan-to-value ratio is less than 80% at least one borrower must have a minimum credit bureau score of 600. Standard credit review and documentation required. (Applies: Alberta, Ontario)",
