        "policy": "Property Taxes",
        "description": "* Property taxes are required to be up to date at time of funding.\r\n* We do not require for the property taxes to be collected with the mortgage payment.\r\n* The client has a choice to set up their taxes with their own municipality\r\n**Property tax accounts Nore**\r\n* we cannot transfer escrow accounts from other lenders. Any amounts in these accounts are deducted from the mortgage balance before the mortgage is paid out and will be reflected on the payout statement. For example, if the mortgage balance is $200,000 and the property tax escrow balance is $2,000, the new Alterna mortgage will be $198,000. Clients are responsible for paying any outstanding property tax balances at the time of transfer. (Applies: Ontario)",
